{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QsnWphYmxwrXR5CkyqjGdo","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Walker Walk baseline seeds 1-2\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"2 additional seeds for dt=1 baseline, establishing per-seed v/e calibration curves\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"seed1_eval_return_55K\": 610,\n7\t      \"seed1_eval_return_105K\": 890,\n8\t      \"seed1_eval_return_last10_mean\": 935,\n9\t      \"seed1_value_eval_ratio_35K\": 0.255,\n10\t      \"seed1_value_eval_ratio_55K\": 0.42,\n11\t      \"seed1_value_eval_ratio_105K\": 0.67,\n12\t      \"seed2_eval_return_55K\": 580,\n13\t      \"seed2_eval_return_105K\": 870,\n14\t      \"seed2_eval_return_last10_mean\": 920,\n15\t      \"seed2_value_eval_ratio_35K\": 0.22,\n16\t      \"seed2_value_eval_ratio_55K\": 0.38,\n17\t      \"seed2_value_eval_ratio_105K\": 0.64,\n18\t      \"cross_seed_mean_last10\": 935,\n19\t      \"cross_seed_std_last10\": 15,\n20\t      \"cross_seed_ve_stable_range\": \"67-74%\"\n21\t    },\n22\t    \"tables\": [\n23\t      {\n24\t        \"name\": \"Baseline v/e calibration (3 seeds)\",\n25\t        \"columns\": [\n26\t          \"step\",\n27\t          \"seed0_ve\",\n28\t          \"seed1_ve\",\n29\t          \"seed2_ve\",\n30\t          \"mean_ve\",\n31\t          \"std_ve\"\n32\t        ],\n33\t        \"rows\": [\n34\t          [\n35\t            \"25K\",\n36\t            0.087,\n37\t            0.095,\n38\t            0.08,\n39\t            0.087,\n40\t            0.006\n41\t          ],\n42\t          [\n43\t            \"35K\",\n44\t            0.241,\n45\t            0.255,\n46\t            0.22,\n47\t            0.239,\n48\t            0.014\n49\t          ],\n50\t          [\n51\t            \"55K\",\n52\t            0.404,\n53\t            0.42,\n54\t            0.38,\n55\t            0.401,\n56\t            0.016\n57\t          ],\n58\t          [\n59\t            \"105K\",\n60\t            0.656,\n61\t            0.67,\n62\t            0.64,\n63\t            0.655,\n64\t            0.012\n65\t          ]\n66\t        ]\n67\t      }\n68\t    ],\n69\t    \"figures\": [],\n70\t    \"analysis\": \"Baseline 的 3-seed 一致性高（CV<2%），为 normalized v/e 的 per-seed 计算提供可靠参考。 v/e stable range 67-74% 跨 seed，比单 seed 的 69-72% 稍宽，但仍是紧致分布。 这意味着 >1.5x normalized v/e 阈值在 3-seed 下仍有足够 margin。\\n\\n\\nWalker Walk dt=1 baseline 在 DreamerV3 中是成熟配置，seed 间 variance 较小。 Seed 0 asymptote 950.9，预期 seed 1-2 在 920-950 范围内（±3%），v/e 稳态在 67-74%。 这是 median 档的正常 baseline variance，不影响因果链判断。 v/e calibration curves 形状一致（单调上升后饱和），但具体数值有 ±0.03 偏移， 这会为后续 normalized v/e 计算引入小幅 per-seed 校准差异。\\n\"\n71\t  },\n72\t  {\n73\t    \"name\": \"Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\",\n74\t    \"description\": \"Replicate delusional critic collapse: subsample ON + trained dt_emb + H=8\",\n75\t    \"results\": {\n76\t      \"seed1_eval_return_25K\": 155,\n77\t      \"seed1_eval_return_35K\": 138,\n78\t      \"seed1_eval_return_45K\": 125,\n79\t      \"seed1_value_eval_ratio_35K\": 0.45,\n80\t      \"seed1_value_eval_ratio_45K\": 0.72,\n81\t      \"seed1_normalized_ve_35K\": 1.76,\n82\t      \"seed1_normalized_ve_45K\": 2.17,\n83\t      \"seed1_verdict\": \"COLLAPSE_CONFIRMED\",\n84\t      \"seed2_eval_return_25K\": 180,\n85\t      \"seed2_eval_return_35K\": 170,\n86\t      \"seed2_eval_return_45K\": 162,\n87\t      \"seed2_value_eval_ratio_35K\": 0.35,\n88\t      \"seed2_value_eval_ratio_45K\": 0.55,\n89\t      \"seed2_normalized_ve_35K\": 1.59,\n90\t      \"seed2_normalized_ve_45K\": 1.66,\n91\t      \"seed2_verdict\": \"DEGRADATION_NO_FULL_COLLAPSE\",\n92\t      \"collapse_replication_count\": 2,\n93\t      \"cross_seed_mean_eval_45K\": 143\n94\t    },\n95\t    \"tables\": [\n96\t      {\n97\t        \"name\": \"008d collapse replication (3 seeds)\",\n98\t        \"columns\": [\n99\t          \"step\",\n100\t          \"seed0_eval\",\n101\t          \"seed1_eval\",\n102\t          \"seed2_eval\",\n103\t          \"seed0_nve\",\n104\t          \"seed1_nve\",\n105\t          \"seed2_nve\"\n106\t        ],\n107\t        \"rows\": [\n108\t          [\n109\t            \"25K\",\n110\t            167,\n111\t            155,\n112\t            180,\n113\t            1.78,\n114\t            1.73,\n115\t            1.52\n116\t          ],\n117\t          [\n118\t            \"35K\",\n119\t            146,\n120\t            138,\n121\t            170,\n122\t            1.71,\n123\t            1.76,\n124\t            1.59\n125\t          ],\n126\t          [\n127\t            \"45K\",\n128\t            141,\n129\t            125,\n130\t            162,\n131\t            2.09,\n132\t            2.17,\n133\t            1.66\n134\t          ]\n135\t        ]\n136\t      }\n137\t    ],\n138\t    \"figures\": [],\n139\t    \"analysis\": \"2/3 seeds 完全 collapse（eval <145@45K + accelerating normalized v/e >2.0x）， 1 seed 显著 degradation 但未 crash（eval 162@45K, normalized v/e 1.66x 仍在 pathological zone 但增速慢）。 这支持 \\\"trained dt_emb is a primary contributing factor\\\" 而非 \\\"deterministic root cause\\\"。 normalized v/e >1.5x 在所有 3 seeds 出现，作为 diagnostic signal 仍然 robust。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心假设：008d collapse 在 2/3 seeds 复现，1 seed 仅 degradation 不 collapse。 Seed 0 已确认 collapse（eval 167→146→141, normalized v/e 1.78x→2.09x）。 Seed 1 预期复现类似 pattern：v/e 加速 diverge，eval 持续下降，构成 collapse。 Seed 2 是 median 档的关键区分点——trained dt_emb 仍导致 elevated normalized v/e（>1.5x）， 但 eval 仅从 180 缓降到 162 而非 crash，v/e 加速率较低。 可能原因：seed 2 的 RSSM 恰好在 dt=2 transition 上学到了稍好的 representation， 使 value overestimation 速度放慢但不消除。这给了足够 signal 说 trained dt_emb 有害， 但 variance 阻止了 \\\"100% collapse\\\" 的强结论，需用 \\\"primary contributing factor\\\" 措辞。\\n\"\n140\t  },\n141\t  {\n142\t    \"name\": \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\",\n143\t    \"description\": \"Replicate causal control: subsample ON + dt_embed_dim=0 + H=8\",\n144\t    \"results\": {\n145\t      \"seed1_eval_return_25K\": 185,\n146\t      \"seed1_eval_return_35K\": 195,\n147\t      \"seed1_eval_return_55K\": 215,\n148\t      \"seed1_normalized_ve_25K\": 0.98,\n149\t      \"seed1_normalized_ve_35K\": 0.78,\n150\t      \"seed1_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.7,\n151\t      \"seed1_verdict\": \"STABLE_NO_COLLAPSE\",\n152\t      \"seed2_eval_return_25K\": 175,\n153\t      \"seed2_eval_return_35K\": 190,\n154\t      \"seed2_eval_return_55K\": 200,\n155\t      \"seed2_normalized_ve_25K\": 1.08,\n156\t      \"seed2_normalized_ve_35K\": 0.85,\n157\t      \"seed2_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.82,\n158\t      \"seed2_verdict\": \"STABLE_NO_COLLAPSE\",\n159\t      \"stable_replication_count\": 3,\n160\t      \"cross_seed_mean_eval_55K\": 207,\n161\t      \"cross_seed_nve_range_55K\": \"0.70-0.82\"\n162\t    },\n163\t    \"tables\": [\n164\t      {\n165\t        \"name\": \"008f stability replication (3 seeds)\",\n166\t        \"columns\": [\n167\t          \"step\",\n168\t          \"seed0_eval\",\n169\t          \"seed1_eval\",\n170\t          \"seed2_eval\",\n171\t          \"seed0_nve\",\n172\t          \"seed1_nve\",\n173\t          \"seed2_nve\"\n174\t        ],\n175\t        \"rows\": [\n176\t          [\n177\t            \"25K\",\n178\t            197,\n179\t            185,\n180\t            175,\n181\t            1.02,\n182\t            0.98,\n183\t            1.08\n184\t          ],\n185\t          [\n186\t            \"35K\",\n187\t            207,\n188\t            195,\n189\t            190,\n190\t            0.73,\n191\t            0.78,\n192\t            0.85\n193\t          ],\n194\t          [\n195\t            \"55K\",\n196\t            210,\n197\t            215,\n198\t            200,\n199\t            0.68,\n200\t            0.7,\n201\t            0.82\n202\t          ]\n203\t        ]\n204\t      }\n205\t    ],\n206\t    \"figures\": [],\n207\t    \"analysis\": \"008f 的 3-seed stability 与 008d 的 2/3-seed collapse 形成鲜明对比。 因果推断仍然成立：在完全相同的 subsample ON + H=8 条件下， 唯一差异（dt_embedding 有/无）决定了 collapse/stable 分野。 即使 008d seed 2 未完全 collapse，其 normalized v/e（1.52-1.66x） 与 008f 全部 seeds 的 nve（0.68-1.08x）之间有明确 gap。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档假设 008f 全程 stable（normalized v/e <1.1x）。 Seed 0 已确认 stable（nve 1.02x@25K→0.73x@35K，下降趋势）。 移除 dt_embedding 后 value function 无法 exploit dt 信息， 因此所有 seeds 都应显示 normalized v/e 收敛到 baseline 水平或以下。 Eval performance 受限于 H=8 + subsample ON（学习信号减少）， 停留在 baseline 的 ~20-22%，但关键是没有 collapse。 3/3 seeds stable 是 median 档的合理预期——因为这是一个 \\\"移除有害因素\\\" 的实验， variance 主要体现在 absolute performance 而非 collapse/non-collapse 的二分上。\\n\"\n208\t  },\n209\t  {\n210\t    \"name\": \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\",\n211\t    \"description\": \"Replicate value growth suppression: subsample OFF + untrained dt_emb + H=15\",\n212\t    \"results\": {\n213\t      \"seed1_eval_return_55K\": 510,\n214\t      \"seed1_eval_return_65K\": 580,\n215\t      \"seed1_eval_return_85K\": 550,\n216\t      \"seed1_eval_return_105K\": 720,\n217\t      \"seed1_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.88,\n218\t      \"seed1_normalized_ve_105K\": 0.65,\n219\t      \"seed1_v_recovery_cycles\": 2,\n220\t      \"seed1_verdict\": \"V_RECOVERY_CONFIRMED\",\n221\t      \"seed2_eval_return_55K\": 460,\n222\t      \"seed2_eval_return_65K\": 530,\n223\t      \"seed2_eval_return_85K\": 520,\n224\t      \"seed2_eval_return_105K\": 580,\n225\t      \"seed2_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.95,\n226\t      \"seed2_normalized_ve_105K\": 0.78,\n227\t      \"seed2_v_recovery_cycles\": 0,\n228\t      \"seed2_verdict\": \"PLATEAU_NO_COLLAPSE\",\n229\t      \"recovery_replication_count\": 2,\n230\t      \"cross_seed_mean_105K\": 693,\n231\t      \"multiseed_mean_105K_range\": \"580-778\"\n232\t    },\n233\t    \"tables\": [\n234\t      {\n235\t        \"name\": \"008a V-recovery replication (3 seeds)\",\n236\t        \"columns\": [\n237\t          \"step\",\n238\t          \"seed0_eval\",\n239\t          \"seed1_eval\",\n240\t          \"seed2_eval\",\n241\t          \"seed0_nve\",\n242\t          \"seed1_nve\",\n243\t          \"seed2_nve\"\n244\t        ],\n245\t        \"rows\": [\n246\t          [\n247\t            \"55K\",\n248\t            488,\n249\t            510,\n250\t            460,\n251\t            0.93,\n252\t            0.88,\n253\t            0.95\n254\t          ],\n255\t          [\n256\t            \"65K\",\n257\t            608,\n258\t            580,\n259\t            530,\n260\t            0.66,\n261\t            0.72,\n262\t            0.8\n263\t          ],\n264\t          [\n265\t            \"85K\",\n266\t            584,\n267\t            550,\n268\t            520,\n269\t            0.68,\n270\t            0.71,\n271\t            0.76\n272\t          ],\n273\t          [\n274\t            \"105K\",\n275\t            778,\n276\t            720,\n277\t            580,\n278\t            0.59,\n279\t            0.65,\n280\t            0.78\n281\t          ]\n282\t        ]\n283\t      }\n284\t    ],\n285\t    \"figures\": [],\n286\t    \"analysis\": \"V-recovery 的 seed variance 迫使将 C3 的表述从 \\\"V-shaped recovery is a signature\\\"  调整为 \\\"untrained dt_emb consistently prevents collapse and suppresses v/e,  with recovery dynamics varying across seeds\\\"。 核心 finding（value suppression → no collapse）在 3/3 seeds robust。 V-recovery 作为 secondary pattern 在 2/3 seeds 出现，可作为 suggestive evidence 而非 strong claim。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档假设：008a V-recovery 在 2/3 seeds 出现，1 seed 仅 plateau 不 recover。 Seed 0 已确认双 V-recovery（501→608→470→778）。 Seed 1 预期类似 pattern：untrained dt_emb 抑制 value overestimation， 允许 actor 在过拟合后恢复，但 peak 略低于 seed 0（720 vs 778）。 Seed 2 是 median 档的区分点——normalized v/e 仍被抑制（<1.0x，无 collapse）， 但 eval return 在 530 附近 plateau 而非形成清晰 V-recovery。 可能机制：seed 2 的 actor 收敛到一个 suboptimal 但 stable 的 policy， value suppression 阻止了 overestimation 但 exploration 不足以跳出 local optimum。 关键是 3/3 seeds 都 no collapse + normalized v/e <1.0x， protective effect 是 robust 的；V-recovery 的具体 pattern 有 seed variance。 cross_seed_mean_105K = (778+720+580)/3 ≈ 693，落在 median 档指标范围 [550,720] 内。\\n\"\n287\t  },\n288\t  {\n289\t    \"name\": \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\",\n290\t    \"description\": \"dt=1 baseline in second DMC environment, establishing Cheetah-specific v/e calibration\",\n291\t    \"results\": {\n292\t      \"seed0_eval_return_55K\": 450,\n293\t      \"seed0_eval_return_105K\": 680,\n294\t      \"seed0_eval_return_asymptotic\": 780,\n295\t      \"seed1_eval_return_55K\": 430,\n296\t      \"seed1_eval_return_105K\": 660,\n297\t      \"seed1_eval_return_asymptotic\": 760,\n298\t      \"seed2_eval_return_55K\": 470,\n299\t      \"seed2_eval_return_105K\": 700,\n300\t      \"seed2_eval_return_asymptotic\": 800,\n301\t      \"mean_eval_return_asymptotic\": 780,\n302\t      \"mean_value_eval_ratio_35K\": 0.19,\n303\t      \"mean_value_eval_ratio_55K\": 0.35,\n304\t      \"mean_value_eval_ratio_105K\": 0.55,\n305\t      \"ve_stable_range\": \"58-65%\"\n306\t    },\n307\t    \"tables\": [\n308\t      {\n309\t        \"name\": \"Cheetah Run baseline v/e calibration (3 seeds)\",\n310\t        \"columns\": [\n311\t          \"step\",\n312\t          \"mean_eval\",\n313\t          \"std_eval\",\n314\t          \"mean_ve\",\n315\t          \"std_ve\"\n316\t        ],\n317\t        \"rows\": [\n318\t          [\n319\t            \"25K\",\n320\t            220,\n321\t            25,\n322\t            0.1,\n323\t            0.02\n324\t          ],\n325\t          [\n326\t            \"35K\",\n327\t            310,\n328\t            20,\n329\t            0.19,\n330\t            0.03\n331\t          ],\n332\t          [\n333\t            \"55K\",\n334\t            450,\n335\t            20,\n336\t            0.35,\n337\t            0.03\n338\t          ],\n339\t          [\n340\t            \"105K\",\n341\t            680,\n342\t            20,\n343\t            0.55,\n344\t            0.04\n345\t          ]\n346\t        ]\n347\t      }\n348\t    ],\n349\t    \"figures\": [],\n350\t    \"analysis\": \"Cheetah baseline 的 v/e asymptote 较低（~60% vs Walker ~70%）， 这将影响 normalized v/e 的解读——同样的 absolute v/e 在 Cheetah 中 normalized 更高。 需要 environment-specific calibration，不能直接复用 Walker 的 1.5x 阈值。\\n\\n\\nCheetah Run 的 DreamerV3 baseline 通常低于 Walker Walk（~780 vs ~950）。 Cheetah Run 的 dynamics 更连续平滑（locomotion on flat terrain）， RSSM 对 Cheetah 的 reconstruction quality 通常优于 Walker（接触力学更简单）。 v/e 稳态 58-65% 略低于 Walker 的 69-72%，反映 Cheetah 的 reward landscape 不同。 3 seeds variance 预期 ±3-5%，略高于 Walker（Cheetah 的 reward 更连续 → 更多 local optima）。\\n\"\n351\t  },\n352\t  {\n353\t    \"name\": \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\",\n354\t    \"description\": \"Replicate delusional critic in Cheetah Run: dt=2 + subsample ON + trained dt_emb + H=8\",\n355\t    \"results\": {\n356\t      \"seed0_eval_return_25K\": 160,\n357\t      \"seed0_eval_return_35K\": 200,\n358\t      \"seed0_eval_return_45K\": 195,\n359\t      \"seed0_eval_return_55K\": 180,\n360\t      \"seed0_normalized_ve_35K\": 1.35,\n361\t      \"seed0_normalized_ve_45K\": 1.45,\n362\t      \"seed0_normalized_ve_55K\": 1.5,\n363\t      \"seed0_verdict\": \"DEGRADATION_BORDERLINE\",\n364\t      \"seed1_eval_return_35K\": 220,\n365\t      \"seed1_eval_return_55K\": 205,\n366\t      \"seed1_normalized_ve_35K\": 1.25,\n367\t      \"seed1_normalized_ve_55K\": 1.38,\n368\t      \"seed1_verdict\": \"DEGRADATION_MILD\",\n369\t      \"seed2_eval_return_35K\": 185,\n370\t      \"seed2_eval_return_55K\": 165,\n371\t      \"seed2_normalized_ve_35K\": 1.4,\n372\t      \"seed2_normalized_ve_55K\": 1.52,\n373\t      \"seed2_verdict\": \"DEGRADATION_BORDERLINE\",\n374\t      \"cross_seed_mean_eval_55K\": 183,\n375\t      \"cheetah_trained_dtEmb_peak_normalized_ve\": 1.35,\n376\t      \"collapse_count\": 0,\n377\t      \"vs_baseline_pct_55K\": \"-59%\"\n378\t    },\n379\t    \"tables\": [\n380\t      {\n381\t        \"name\": \"Cheetah trained dt_emb (3 seeds) vs Walker 008d\",\n382\t        \"columns\": [\n383\t          \"env\",\n384\t          \"step\",\n385\t          \"mean_eval\",\n386\t          \"mean_nve\",\n387\t          \"walker_008d_nve\",\n388\t          \"gap\"\n389\t        ],\n390\t        \"rows\": [\n391\t          [\n392\t            \"Cheetah\",\n393\t            \"25K\",\n394\t            170,\n395\t            1.2,\n396\t            1.78,\n397\t            \"-0.58x\"\n398\t          ],\n399\t          [\n400\t            \"Cheetah\",\n401\t            \"35K\",\n402\t            202,\n403\t            1.33,\n404\t            1.71,\n405\t            \"-0.38x\"\n406\t          ],\n407\t          [\n408\t            \"Cheetah\",\n409\t            \"45K\",\n410\t            195,\n411\t            1.42,\n412\t            2.09,\n413\t            \"-0.67x\"\n414\t          ],\n415\t          [\n416\t            \"Cheetah\",\n417\t            \"55K\",\n418\t            183,\n419\t            1.47,\n420\t            \"N/A (collapsed)\",\n421\t            \"—\"\n422\t          ]\n423\t        ]\n424\t      }\n425\t    ],\n426\t    \"figures\": [],\n427\t    \"analysis\": \"Cheetah 的 trained dt_emb 效果是 \\\"attenuated Walker\\\" 而非 \\\"clean replication\\\"。 这是 median 档的核心挑战：collapse 不复现，但 degradation 和 elevated v/e 复现。 需要 reframe C2：dt_embedding 的危害程度由 RSSM fidelity at dt>1 调节。 Walker 的 contact dynamics → 高 RSSM error → 快速 collapse。 Cheetah 的 smooth dynamics → 低 RSSM error → 慢速 degradation。 v/e overshoot ratio >1.5x 阈值在 Cheetah 中不是硬界限而是 \\\"warning zone\\\"。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心假设：Cheetah Run 中 trained dt_emb 降性能但 collapse 不如 Walker 剧烈 （normalized v/e 1.2-1.5x，边界区）。 机制：Cheetah 的 dynamics 比 Walker 更平滑连续，RSSM 在 dt=2 的 prediction error 较低。 因此 trained dt_emb 导致的 value overestimation 速度更慢、幅度更小。 normalized v/e 在 1.2-1.5x 区间——超过 baseline 但未达到 Walker 的 >2.0x 加速 diverge。 Eval return 呈缓慢下降趋势（200→180）而非 Walker 的急剧 collapse（167→141）。 这产生了关键的 \\\"environment-dependent modulation\\\" 叙事： 相同的 dt_embedding 机制在不同 RSSM fidelity 条件下产生不同严重程度。 从方法论看，这其实 *strengthens* 而非 weakens 因果解释—— 因为它指向 RSSM prediction quality 作为调节变量，与 C2 机制一致。\\n\"\n428\t  },\n429\t  {\n430\t    \"name\": \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\",\n431\t    \"description\": \"Causal control in Cheetah: dt=2 + subsample ON + dt_embed_dim=0 + H=8\",\n432\t    \"results\": {\n433\t      \"seed0_eval_return_35K\": 195,\n434\t      \"seed0_eval_return_55K\": 220,\n435\t      \"seed0_normalized_ve_35K\": 0.82,\n436\t      \"seed0_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.75,\n437\t      \"seed1_eval_return_55K\": 210,\n438\t      \"seed1_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.8,\n439\t      \"seed2_eval_return_55K\": 230,\n440\t      \"seed2_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.72,\n441\t      \"cross_seed_mean_eval_55K\": 220,\n442\t      \"cross_seed_mean_nve_55K\": 0.76,\n443\t      \"cheetah_no_dtEmb_normalized_ve\": 0.76,\n444\t      \"vs_baseline_pct_55K\": \"-51%\",\n445\t      \"vs_trained_dtEmb_gap_eval\": \"+37 (220 vs 183)\",\n446\t      \"vs_trained_dtEmb_gap_nve\": \"-0.71x (0.76 vs 1.47)\"\n447\t    },\n448\t    \"tables\": [\n449\t      {\n450\t        \"name\": \"Cheetah 008f-equivalent vs trained dt_emb (mean across 3 seeds)\",\n451\t        \"columns\": [\n452\t          \"config\",\n453\t          \"eval_55K\",\n454\t          \"nve_55K\",\n455\t          \"collapse\"\n456\t        ],\n457\t        \"rows\": [\n458\t          [\n459\t            \"trained dt_emb\",\n460\t            183,\n461\t            1.47,\n462\t            \"degradation (no collapse)\"\n463\t          ],\n464\t          [\n465\t            \"dt_embed_dim=0\",\n466\t            220,\n467\t            0.76,\n468\t            \"no degradation\"\n469\t          ],\n470\t          [\n471\t            \"baseline\",\n472\t            450,\n473\t            \"1.0 (reference)\",\n474\t            \"N/A\"\n475\t          ]\n476\t        ]\n477\t      }\n478\t    ],\n479\t    \"figures\": [],\n480\t    \"analysis\": \"因果方向在 Cheetah 仍成立（removing dt_emb → lower v/e + better performance）， 但 effect size 是 Walker 的约 50%。这是论文中 \\\"boundary conditions\\\" section 的核心数据： 当 RSSM prediction quality 较好时（Cheetah），dt_embedding 的危害减轻但不消失。 cheetah_no_dtEmb_normalized_ve=0.76 落在 median 档指标范围 [0.7, 1.15] 内。\\n\\n\\n移除 dt_embedding 在 Cheetah 中同样消除 elevated v/e，但 performance gap 较 Walker 小。 在 Walker 中，008f vs 008d 的 eval gap 明显（207 vs 141@55K）。 在 Cheetah 中，gap 缩小（220 vs 183@55K），因为 baseline degradation 本身较温和。 Normalized v/e 在 0.7-1.15x 范围（median 档指标），低于 1.0x 表示 no overestimation。 因果方向仍一致（有 dt_emb → nve>1.2x, 无 dt_emb → nve<1.0x），但 effect size 较小。 这支持 \\\"dt_embedding is harmful but severity is environment-modulated\\\"。\\n\"\n481\t  },\n482\t  {\n483\t    \"name\": \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\",\n484\t    \"description\": \"Value growth suppression in Cheetah: dt=2 + subsample OFF + untrained dt_emb + H=15\",\n485\t    \"results\": {\n486\t      \"seed0_eval_return_55K\": 380,\n487\t      \"seed0_eval_return_105K\": 550,\n488\t      \"seed0_normalized_ve_105K\": 0.72,\n489\t      \"seed1_eval_return_105K\": 520,\n490\t      \"seed1_normalized_ve_105K\": 0.78,\n491\t      \"seed2_eval_return_105K\": 490,\n492\t      \"seed2_normalized_ve_105K\": 0.82,\n493\t      \"cross_seed_mean_105K\": 520,\n494\t      \"vs_baseline_pct_105K\": \"-24%\",\n495\t      \"v_recovery_count\": \"1/3 seeds shows V-recovery, 2/3 plateau\",\n496\t      \"cheetah_best_dt2_vs_baseline_pct\": \"67%\"\n497\t    },\n498\t    \"tables\": [\n499\t      {\n500\t        \"name\": \"Cheetah untrained dt_emb recovery (3 seeds)\",\n501\t        \"columns\": [\n502\t          \"step\",\n503\t          \"seed0\",\n504\t          \"seed1\",\n505\t          \"seed2\",\n506\t          \"mean\",\n507\t          \"nve_mean\"\n508\t        ],\n509\t        \"rows\": [\n510\t          [\n511\t            \"55K\",\n512\t            380,\n513\t            360,\n514\t            350,\n515\t            363,\n516\t            0.88\n517\t          ],\n518\t          [\n519\t            \"75K\",\n520\t            420,\n521\t            440,\n522\t            410,\n523\t            423,\n524\t            0.82\n525\t          ],\n526\t          [\n527\t            \"105K\",\n528\t            550,\n529\t            520,\n530\t            490,\n531\t            520,\n532\t            0.77\n533\t          ]\n534\t        ]\n535\t      }\n536\t    ],\n537\t    \"figures\": [],\n538\t    \"analysis\": \"Cheetah 的 untrained dt_emb configuration 确认 protective effect（no collapse, nve<1.0x） 但 recovery 更缓慢。这与 environment-dependent modulation 假设一致： Cheetah 的 RSSM error 较低 → dt_emb 的影响（有害或保护性的）都被 attenuate。 论文中可用此数据支持 \\\"the dt_embedding mechanism is general,  but its magnitude scales with RSSM prediction error\\\"。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档假设：Cheetah 中 untrained dt_emb 有保护作用但 gap 较小。 Walker 中 008a 达 baseline 85%（778/916），Cheetah 预期只达 67%（520/780）。 原因：Cheetah 的 smooth dynamics 使 RSSM error 较低 → trained dt_emb 的危害本就较小 →  untrained dt_emb 的 \\\"保护效果\\\" 相对 margin 也较小（从 183 到 220 vs 从 141 到 207 in Walker）。 V-recovery pattern 在 Cheetah 中更弱：只有 1/3 seeds 出现， 因为 Cheetah 的 reward landscape 更平 → actor 倾向 plateau 而非 oscillate。 cheetah_best_dt2_vs_baseline_pct=67% 落在 median 档指标范围 [50%, 75%] 内。\\n\"\n539\t  },\n540\t  {\n541\t    \"name\": \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\",\n542\t    \"description\": \"Measure observation/reward reconstruction loss at dt=2 vs dt=1 from existing trained models across both environments\",\n543\t    \"results\": {\n544\t      \"walker_rssm_recon_loss_dt1\": 4.2,\n545\t      \"walker_rssm_recon_loss_dt2\": 6.8,\n546\t      \"walker_dt2_dt1_ratio\": 1.62,\n547\t      \"cheetah_rssm_recon_loss_dt1\": 3.9,\n548\t      \"cheetah_rssm_recon_loss_dt2\": 5.1,\n549\t      \"cheetah_dt2_dt1_ratio\": 1.31,\n550\t      \"walker_reward_pred_error_dt1\": 0.08,\n551\t      \"walker_reward_pred_error_dt2\": 0.25,\n552\t      \"cheetah_reward_pred_error_dt1\": 0.06,\n553\t      \"cheetah_reward_pred_error_dt2\": 0.12,\n554\t      \"cross_env_recon_gap_ratio\": 1.24\n555\t    },\n556\t    \"tables\": [\n557\t      {\n558\t        \"name\": \"RSSM reconstruction loss: dt=1 vs dt=2 × environment\",\n559\t        \"columns\": [\n560\t          \"environment\",\n561\t          \"loss_dt1\",\n562\t          \"loss_dt2\",\n563\t          \"ratio\",\n564\t          \"reward_err_dt1\",\n565\t          \"reward_err_dt2\",\n566\t          \"reward_ratio\"\n567\t        ],\n568\t        \"rows\": [\n569\t          [\n570\t            \"Walker Walk\",\n571\t            4.2,\n572\t            6.8,\n573\t            1.62,\n574\t            0.08,\n575\t            0.25,\n576\t            3.13\n577\t          ],\n578\t          [\n579\t            \"Cheetah Run\",\n580\t            3.9,\n581\t            5.1,\n582\t            1.31,\n583\t            0.06,\n584\t            0.12,\n585\t            2.0\n586\t          ]\n587\t        ]\n588\t      }\n589\t    ],\n590\t    \"figures\": [],\n591\t    \"analysis\": \"plan_030 提供了 \\\"environment-dependent modulation\\\" 假设的 mechanistic foundation。 Walker 的 RSSM dt2/dt1 gap 比 Cheetah 大 ~24%（1.62/1.31=1.24x）， 这与 Walker 中 trained dt_emb 导致更严重 collapse 的观察一致。 但只有两个环境点，无法建立 quantitative 关系。 论文中应呈现为 \\\"consistent with the hypothesis\\\" 而非 \\\"proves\\\"。 如果 plan_040（Hopper Hop）执行，将提供第三个点。\\n\\n\\n这是 median 档叙事的关键支撑实验——直接量化 RSSM fidelity gap 的 environment dependence。 Walker Walk 涉及 contact dynamics（脚与地面碰撞），dt=2 跳过一个接触事件时 RSSM 需要 \\\"想象\\\" 中间状态，reconstruction loss 预期升高 ~60%（ratio 1.6x）。 Cheetah Run 的 dynamics 更平滑（无离散接触切换）， dt=2 的 prediction 误差增幅较小（~30%, ratio 1.3x）。 这个 1.6x vs 1.3x 的差距直接解释了为什么 trained dt_emb 在 Walker 导致 collapse  而在 Cheetah 仅导致 degradation：更大的 RSSM error → 更多 delusional critic gradient → 更快 collapse。 Reward prediction error 的环境间差异更大（3.1x vs 2.0x ratio）， 因为 Walker 的 reward 与接触事件强耦合。\\n\"\n592\t  },\n593\t  {\n594\t    \"name\": \"Actor entropy analysis\",\n595\t    \"description\": \"Plot actor entropy vs training step for healthy (008a/008c/008f) vs collapsed (006/008d) configurations\",\n596\t    \"results\": {\n597\t      \"walker_008d_entropy_25K\": 3.8,\n598\t      \"walker_008d_entropy_35K\": 4.1,\n599\t      \"walker_008d_entropy_45K\": 4.5,\n600\t      \"walker_008d_entropy_trend\": \"increasing\",\n601\t      \"walker_006_entropy_35K\": 3.9,\n602\t      \"walker_006_entropy_55K\": 5.2,\n603\t      \"walker_006_entropy_trend\": \"sharply_increasing\",\n604\t      \"walker_008a_entropy_55K\": 3.2,\n605\t      \"walker_008a_entropy_105K\": 2.8,\n606\t      \"walker_008a_entropy_trend\": \"stable_to_decreasing\",\n607\t      \"walker_008f_entropy_35K\": 3.5,\n608\t      \"walker_008f_entropy_trend\": \"stable\",\n609\t      \"walker_baseline_entropy_35K\": 3.0,\n610\t      \"walker_baseline_entropy_105K\": 2.5,\n611\t      \"walker_baseline_entropy_trend\": \"decreasing\"\n612\t    },\n613\t    \"tables\": [\n614\t      {\n615\t        \"name\": \"Actor entropy trajectories\",\n616\t        \"columns\": [\n617\t          \"config\",\n618\t          \"entropy_25K\",\n619\t          \"entropy_35K\",\n620\t          \"entropy_45K\",\n621\t          \"entropy_55K\",\n622\t          \"trend\"\n623\t        ],\n624\t        \"rows\": [\n625\t          [\n626\t            \"baseline\",\n627\t            3.2,\n628\t            3.0,\n629\t            2.9,\n630\t            2.8,\n631\t            \"decreasing\"\n632\t          ],\n633\t          [\n634\t            \"008d (collapse)\",\n635\t            3.8,\n636\t            4.1,\n637\t            4.5,\n638\t            \"—\",\n639\t            \"increasing\"\n640\t          ],\n641\t          [\n642\t            \"006 (collapse)\",\n643\t            3.5,\n644\t            3.9,\n645\t            4.2,\n646\t            5.2,\n647\t            \"sharply increasing\"\n648\t          ],\n649\t          [\n650\t            \"008a (V-recovery)\",\n651\t            3.3,\n652\t            3.1,\n653\t            3.0,\n654\t            3.2,\n655\t            \"stable\"\n656\t          ],\n657\t          [\n658\t            \"008f (stable)\",\n659\t            3.4,\n660\t            3.5,\n661\t            3.3,\n662\t            \"—\",\n663\t            \"stable\"\n664\t          ]\n665\t        ]\n666\t      }\n667\t    ],\n668\t    \"figures\": [],\n669\t    \"analysis\": \"Entropy analysis 为 C2 提供 corroborating evidence 而非 primary evidence。 Collapsed configs 的 entropy 上升模式与 \\\"delusional critic → actor confusion\\\" 一致。 在 paper 中作为 supplementary figure 或 appendix，支撑 main text 的 causal diagram。\\n\\n\\nActor entropy 增高表示 policy 变得更随机——这是 delusional critic gradient 的下游症状。 当 value function 高估 → actor 收到 misleading gradient → policy 不再有 clear preference → entropy 升高。 预期 collapsed configs（008d, 006）显示 entropy 单调上升（actor confusion）， 而 healthy configs（008a, 008f, baseline）显示 entropy stable 或下降（policy sharpening）。 这不是新发现，但提供了 mechanism 的额外 sanity check： 如果 collapsed configs 的 entropy *不*上升，则 C2 的 \\\"delusional critic → actor degradation\\\" 链需要修正。 Median 档下预期 pattern 清晰但 noise 较大（因为 entropy 是 high-variance metric）。\\n\"\n670\t  },\n671\t  {\n672\t    \"name\": \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\",\n673\t    \"description\": \"Distribution plots of V(s) vs Monte Carlo return for trained vs untrained dt_emb\",\n674\t    \"results\": {\n675\t      \"walker_008d_value_mc_correlation\": 0.35,\n676\t      \"walker_008d_value_bias\": \"+45% (systematic overestimation)\",\n677\t      \"walker_008d_value_std_ratio\": 2.1,\n678\t      \"walker_008a_value_mc_correlation\": 0.72,\n679\t      \"walker_008a_value_bias\": \"+8% (mild overestimation)\",\n680\t      \"walker_008a_value_std_ratio\": 1.2,\n681\t      \"walker_baseline_value_mc_correlation\": 0.85,\n682\t      \"walker_baseline_value_bias\": \"+5%\",\n683\t      \"walker_baseline_value_std_ratio\": 1.1,\n684\t      \"walker_008f_value_mc_correlation\": 0.68,\n685\t      \"walker_008f_value_bias\": \"+10%\",\n686\t      \"walker_008f_value_std_ratio\": 1.3\n687\t    },\n688\t    \"tables\": [\n689\t      {\n690\t        \"name\": \"Value calibration summary\",\n691\t        \"columns\": [\n692\t          \"config\",\n693\t          \"correlation\",\n694\t          \"bias_pct\",\n695\t          \"variance_ratio\",\n696\t          \"verdict\"\n697\t        ],\n698\t        \"rows\": [\n699\t          [\n700\t            \"baseline\",\n701\t            0.85,\n702\t            \"+5%\",\n703\t            1.1,\n704\t            \"calibrated\"\n705\t          ],\n706\t          [\n707\t            \"008a (untrained)\",\n708\t            0.72,\n709\t            \"+8%\",\n710\t            1.2,\n711\t            \"mildly_optimistic\"\n712\t          ],\n713\t          [\n714\t            \"008f (no dt_emb)\",\n715\t            0.68,\n716\t            \"+10%\",\n717\t            1.3,\n718\t            \"mildly_optimistic\"\n719\t          ],\n720\t          [\n721\t            \"008d (trained)\",\n722\t            0.35,\n723\t            \"+45%\",\n724\t            2.1,\n725\t            \"delusional\"\n726\t          ]\n727\t        ]\n728\t      }\n729\t    ],\n730\t    \"figures\": [],\n731\t    \"analysis\": \"Distribution analysis 将 v/e ratio proxy 升级为更 rigorous 的 value calibration 证据。 008d 的 correlation=0.35 和 bias=+45% 直接证明 \\\"delusional\\\"——value function 的预测 与实际 return 几乎 decouple 且系统性偏高。 这是 paper 中最强的 supplementary evidence，值得在 main text 中给一段或一个 figure。\\n\\n\\nV(s) vs MC return 的联合分布揭示 v/e ratio 无法捕捉的细节。 008d（trained dt_emb, collapse）预期显示：(a) systematic positive bias（值线远高于 y=x）， (b) 低相关性（value 与实际 return decouple），(c) 高 variance ratio（value 在不确定状态大幅波动）。 这三个特征共同构成 \\\"delusional critic\\\" 的 distributional fingerprint。 008a/008f（healthy configs）预期接近 baseline 分布，bias 小、相关性高。 Median 档下预期 pattern 清晰但 008f 的 correlation 略低于 baseline （因为 dt=2 imagination 本身引入了一些 noise，即使没有 dt_embedding）。\\n\"\n732\t  },\n733\t  {\n734\t    \"name\": \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\",\n735\t    \"description\": \"Analyze learned dt_embedding vectors: cosine similarity between dt=1 and dt=2\",\n736\t    \"results\": {\n737\t      \"cosine_sim_5K\": 0.92,\n738\t      \"cosine_sim_15K\": 0.75,\n739\t      \"cosine_sim_35K\": 0.42,\n740\t      \"cosine_sim_55K\": 0.28,\n741\t      \"embedding_norm_dt1_35K\": 1.2,\n742\t      \"embedding_norm_dt2_35K\": 2.8,\n743\t      \"embedding_divergence_onset\": \"~15K-25K (coincides with v/e acceleration)\"\n744\t    },\n745\t    \"tables\": [\n746\t      {\n747\t        \"name\": \"dt_embedding evolution during training\",\n748\t        \"columns\": [\n749\t          \"step\",\n750\t          \"cosine_sim\",\n751\t          \"norm_dt1\",\n752\t          \"norm_dt2\",\n753\t          \"nve_at_step\"\n754\t        ],\n755\t        \"rows\": [\n756\t          [\n757\t            \"5K\",\n758\t            0.92,\n759\t            0.8,\n760\t            0.9,\n761\t            \"~1.0x\"\n762\t          ],\n763\t          [\n764\t            \"15K\",\n765\t            0.75,\n766\t            1.0,\n767\t            1.4,\n768\t            \"~1.2x\"\n769\t          ],\n770\t          [\n771\t            \"25K\",\n772\t            0.55,\n773\t            1.1,\n774\t            2.1,\n775\t            \"~1.5x\"\n776\t          ],\n777\t          [\n778\t            \"35K\",\n779\t            0.42,\n780\t            1.2,\n781\t            2.8,\n782\t            \"~1.7x\"\n783\t          ]\n784\t        ]\n785\t      }\n786\t    ],\n787\t    \"figures\": [],\n788\t    \"analysis\": \"Cosine similarity 分析提供 mechanistic timeline：embedding 分离 → value exploitation → collapse。 这是 P2 priority 因为它补充而非替代 core evidence， 但在论文中可以做一个很有说服力的 timeline figure。 如果 embedding 的分离时间与 v/e 加速不吻合，则 C2 的 mechanism story 需要修正。\\n\\n\\nTrained dt_embedding 在训练过程中逐步学会区分 dt=1 和 dt=2。 早期（<10K）dt=1 和 dt=2 embedding 相似（cosine~0.9），value function 尚未 exploit 差异。 15-25K 时 embedding 开始分离（cosine 下降到 0.5-0.7）， 这恰好与 v/e ratio 开始加速的时间窗口吻合。 这提供了 temporal evidence：dt_embedding 的学习 → value function 开始 exploit → overestimation → collapse。 dt=2 embedding 的 norm 增大（2.8 vs dt=1 的 1.2）表明 value function 放大了 dt=2 的表征， 可能因为 dt=2 transition 在 imagination 中产生更大的 \\\"value opportunity\\\"（但实际是虚假的）。\\n\"\n789\t  },\n790\t  {\n791\t    \"name\": \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\",\n792\t    \"description\": \"Third DMC environment: baseline + trained dt_emb + dt_embed_dim=0\",\n793\t    \"results\": {\n794\t      \"baseline_asymptotic\": 250,\n795\t      \"trained_dtEmb_peak\": 120,\n796\t      \"trained_dtEmb_nve_peak\": 1.55,\n797\t      \"trained_dtEmb_collapse\": \"partial (1/3 seeds collapse, 2/3 degradation)\",\n798\t      \"no_dtEmb_eval_55K\": 105,\n799\t      \"no_dtEmb_nve_55K\": 0.85,\n800\t      \"baseline_ve_stable\": \"55-62%\"\n801\t    },\n802\t    \"tables\": [\n803\t      {\n804\t        \"name\": \"Hopper Hop results summary\",\n805\t        \"columns\": [\n806\t          \"config\",\n807\t          \"mean_eval_55K\",\n808\t          \"mean_nve_55K\",\n809\t          \"collapse_fraction\"\n810\t        ],\n811\t        \"rows\": [\n812\t          [\n813\t            \"baseline\",\n814\t            180,\n815\t            \"1.0 (ref)\",\n816\t            \"0/3\"\n817\t          ],\n818\t          [\n819\t            \"trained dt_emb\",\n820\t            95,\n821\t            1.55,\n822\t            \"1/3\"\n823\t          ],\n824\t          [\n825\t            \"dt_embed_dim=0\",\n826\t            105,\n827\t            0.85,\n828\t            \"0/3\"\n829\t          ]\n830\t        ]\n831\t      }\n832\t    ],\n833\t    \"figures\": [],\n834\t    \"analysis\": \"Hopper 作为第三环境，主要贡献是验证 environment-dependent modulation 假设。 如果 RSSM dt2/dt1 ratio 介于 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间（如 plan_030 预测）， 且 normalized v/e 也介于两者之间，则三个点落在一条正相关趋势线上—— 这将 \\\"environment-dependent modulation\\\" 从 post-hoc 假设升级为 empirical pattern。 但 P2 priority 意味着在 CoRL deadline 前可能无法完成。 Median 档论文即使没有 Hopper 也可以成立，用 Discussion 中的 \\\"boundary conditions\\\" 段覆盖。\\n\\nHopper Hop 是高难度 DMC task（baseline ~250 远低于 Walker ~950 和 Cheetah ~780）。 RSSM prediction quality 介于 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间 （有 hopping contact events 但比 walking 更规律）。 Median 档下预期 trained dt_emb 的 normalized v/e 在 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间（~1.5x）， 1/3 seeds collapse，2/3 degradation。 dt_embed_dim=0 仍应 stable（nve <1.0x）。 但 Hopper 的 absolute performance 很低，signal-to-noise ratio 差 →  结论 less conclusive，主要价值是提供 plan_030 scatter plot 的第三个点。 P2 priority，论文如时间不够可省略。\\n\"\n835\t  }\n836\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e39ae06-ebff-4a82-a634-fdad224fbc5c","uuid":"f56bfd2d-cf32-4db9-ba9c-84fc0ae0eb0f","timestamp":"2026-05-14T06:46:34.701Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_9/projects/event-gated-adaptive-horizon/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T062606/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Walker Walk baseline seeds 1-2\",\n    \"description\": \"2 additional seeds for dt=1 baseline, establishing per-seed v/e calibration curves\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed1_eval_return_55K\": 610,\n      \"seed1_eval_return_105K\": 890,\n      \"seed1_eval_return_last10_mean\": 935,\n      \"seed1_value_eval_ratio_35K\": 0.255,\n      \"seed1_value_eval_ratio_55K\": 0.42,\n      \"seed1_value_eval_ratio_105K\": 0.67,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_55K\": 580,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_105K\": 870,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_last10_mean\": 920,\n      \"seed2_value_eval_ratio_35K\": 0.22,\n      \"seed2_value_eval_ratio_55K\": 0.38,\n      \"seed2_value_eval_ratio_105K\": 0.64,\n      \"cross_seed_mean_last10\": 935,\n      \"cross_seed_std_last10\": 15,\n      \"cross_seed_ve_stable_range\": \"67-74%\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Baseline v/e calibration (3 seeds)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"step\",\n          \"seed0_ve\",\n          \"seed1_ve\",\n          \"seed2_ve\",\n          \"mean_ve\",\n          \"std_ve\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"25K\",\n            0.087,\n            0.095,\n            0.08,\n            0.087,\n            0.006\n          ],\n          [\n            \"35K\",\n            0.241,\n            0.255,\n            0.22,\n            0.239,\n            0.014\n          ],\n          [\n            \"55K\",\n            0.404,\n            0.42,\n            0.38,\n            0.401,\n            0.016\n          ],\n          [\n            \"105K\",\n            0.656,\n            0.67,\n            0.64,\n            0.655,\n            0.012\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Baseline 的 3-seed 一致性高（CV<2%），为 normalized v/e 的 per-seed 计算提供可靠参考。 v/e stable range 67-74% 跨 seed，比单 seed 的 69-72% 稍宽，但仍是紧致分布。 这意味着 >1.5x normalized v/e 阈值在 3-seed 下仍有足够 margin。\\n\\n\\nWalker Walk dt=1 baseline 在 DreamerV3 中是成熟配置，seed 间 variance 较小。 Seed 0 asymptote 950.9，预期 seed 1-2 在 920-950 范围内（±3%），v/e 稳态在 67-74%。 这是 median 档的正常 baseline variance，不影响因果链判断。 v/e calibration curves 形状一致（单调上升后饱和），但具体数值有 ±0.03 偏移， 这会为后续 normalized v/e 计算引入小幅 per-seed 校准差异。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\",\n    \"description\": \"Replicate delusional critic collapse: subsample ON + trained dt_emb + H=8\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed1_eval_return_25K\": 155,\n      \"seed1_eval_return_35K\": 138,\n      \"seed1_eval_return_45K\": 125,\n      \"seed1_value_eval_ratio_35K\": 0.45,\n      \"seed1_value_eval_ratio_45K\": 0.72,\n      \"seed1_normalized_ve_35K\": 1.76,\n      \"seed1_normalized_ve_45K\": 2.17,\n      \"seed1_verdict\": \"COLLAPSE_CONFIRMED\",\n      \"seed2_eval_return_25K\": 180,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_35K\": 170,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_45K\": 162,\n      \"seed2_value_eval_ratio_35K\": 0.35,\n      \"seed2_value_eval_ratio_45K\": 0.55,\n      \"seed2_normalized_ve_35K\": 1.59,\n      \"seed2_normalized_ve_45K\": 1.66,\n      \"seed2_verdict\": \"DEGRADATION_NO_FULL_COLLAPSE\",\n      \"collapse_replication_count\": 2,\n      \"cross_seed_mean_eval_45K\": 143\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"008d collapse replication (3 seeds)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"step\",\n          \"seed0_eval\",\n          \"seed1_eval\",\n          \"seed2_eval\",\n          \"seed0_nve\",\n          \"seed1_nve\",\n          \"seed2_nve\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"25K\",\n            167,\n            155,\n            180,\n            1.78,\n            1.73,\n            1.52\n          ],\n          [\n            \"35K\",\n            146,\n            138,\n            170,\n            1.71,\n            1.76,\n            1.59\n          ],\n          [\n            \"45K\",\n            141,\n            125,\n            162,\n            2.09,\n            2.17,\n            1.66\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"2/3 seeds 完全 collapse（eval <145@45K + accelerating normalized v/e >2.0x）， 1 seed 显著 degradation 但未 crash（eval 162@45K, normalized v/e 1.66x 仍在 pathological zone 但增速慢）。 这支持 \\\"trained dt_emb is a primary contributing factor\\\" 而非 \\\"deterministic root cause\\\"。 normalized v/e >1.5x 在所有 3 seeds 出现，作为 diagnostic signal 仍然 robust。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心假设：008d collapse 在 2/3 seeds 复现，1 seed 仅 degradation 不 collapse。 Seed 0 已确认 collapse（eval 167→146→141, normalized v/e 1.78x→2.09x）。 Seed 1 预期复现类似 pattern：v/e 加速 diverge，eval 持续下降，构成 collapse。 Seed 2 是 median 档的关键区分点——trained dt_emb 仍导致 elevated normalized v/e（>1.5x）， 但 eval 仅从 180 缓降到 162 而非 crash，v/e 加速率较低。 可能原因：seed 2 的 RSSM 恰好在 dt=2 transition 上学到了稍好的 representation， 使 value overestimation 速度放慢但不消除。这给了足够 signal 说 trained dt_emb 有害， 但 variance 阻止了 \\\"100% collapse\\\" 的强结论，需用 \\\"primary contributing factor\\\" 措辞。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\",\n    \"description\": \"Replicate causal control: subsample ON + dt_embed_dim=0 + H=8\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed1_eval_return_25K\": 185,\n      \"seed1_eval_return_35K\": 195,\n      \"seed1_eval_return_55K\": 215,\n      \"seed1_normalized_ve_25K\": 0.98,\n      \"seed1_normalized_ve_35K\": 0.78,\n      \"seed1_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.7,\n      \"seed1_verdict\": \"STABLE_NO_COLLAPSE\",\n      \"seed2_eval_return_25K\": 175,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_35K\": 190,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_55K\": 200,\n      \"seed2_normalized_ve_25K\": 1.08,\n      \"seed2_normalized_ve_35K\": 0.85,\n      \"seed2_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.82,\n      \"seed2_verdict\": \"STABLE_NO_COLLAPSE\",\n      \"stable_replication_count\": 3,\n      \"cross_seed_mean_eval_55K\": 207,\n      \"cross_seed_nve_range_55K\": \"0.70-0.82\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"008f stability replication (3 seeds)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"step\",\n          \"seed0_eval\",\n          \"seed1_eval\",\n          \"seed2_eval\",\n          \"seed0_nve\",\n          \"seed1_nve\",\n          \"seed2_nve\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"25K\",\n            197,\n            185,\n            175,\n            1.02,\n            0.98,\n            1.08\n          ],\n          [\n            \"35K\",\n            207,\n            195,\n            190,\n            0.73,\n            0.78,\n            0.85\n          ],\n          [\n            \"55K\",\n            210,\n            215,\n            200,\n            0.68,\n            0.7,\n            0.82\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"008f 的 3-seed stability 与 008d 的 2/3-seed collapse 形成鲜明对比。 因果推断仍然成立：在完全相同的 subsample ON + H=8 条件下， 唯一差异（dt_embedding 有/无）决定了 collapse/stable 分野。 即使 008d seed 2 未完全 collapse，其 normalized v/e（1.52-1.66x） 与 008f 全部 seeds 的 nve（0.68-1.08x）之间有明确 gap。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档假设 008f 全程 stable（normalized v/e <1.1x）。 Seed 0 已确认 stable（nve 1.02x@25K→0.73x@35K，下降趋势）。 移除 dt_embedding 后 value function 无法 exploit dt 信息， 因此所有 seeds 都应显示 normalized v/e 收敛到 baseline 水平或以下。 Eval performance 受限于 H=8 + subsample ON（学习信号减少）， 停留在 baseline 的 ~20-22%，但关键是没有 collapse。 3/3 seeds stable 是 median 档的合理预期——因为这是一个 \\\"移除有害因素\\\" 的实验， variance 主要体现在 absolute performance 而非 collapse/non-collapse 的二分上。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\",\n    \"description\": \"Replicate value growth suppression: subsample OFF + untrained dt_emb + H=15\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed1_eval_return_55K\": 510,\n      \"seed1_eval_return_65K\": 580,\n      \"seed1_eval_return_85K\": 550,\n      \"seed1_eval_return_105K\": 720,\n      \"seed1_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.88,\n      \"seed1_normalized_ve_105K\": 0.65,\n      \"seed1_v_recovery_cycles\": 2,\n      \"seed1_verdict\": \"V_RECOVERY_CONFIRMED\",\n      \"seed2_eval_return_55K\": 460,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_65K\": 530,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_85K\": 520,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_105K\": 580,\n      \"seed2_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.95,\n      \"seed2_normalized_ve_105K\": 0.78,\n      \"seed2_v_recovery_cycles\": 0,\n      \"seed2_verdict\": \"PLATEAU_NO_COLLAPSE\",\n      \"recovery_replication_count\": 2,\n      \"cross_seed_mean_105K\": 693,\n      \"multiseed_mean_105K_range\": \"580-778\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"008a V-recovery replication (3 seeds)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"step\",\n          \"seed0_eval\",\n          \"seed1_eval\",\n          \"seed2_eval\",\n          \"seed0_nve\",\n          \"seed1_nve\",\n          \"seed2_nve\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"55K\",\n            488,\n            510,\n            460,\n            0.93,\n            0.88,\n            0.95\n          ],\n          [\n            \"65K\",\n            608,\n            580,\n            530,\n            0.66,\n            0.72,\n            0.8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"85K\",\n            584,\n            550,\n            520,\n            0.68,\n            0.71,\n            0.76\n          ],\n          [\n            \"105K\",\n            778,\n            720,\n            580,\n            0.59,\n            0.65,\n            0.78\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"V-recovery 的 seed variance 迫使将 C3 的表述从 \\\"V-shaped recovery is a signature\\\"  调整为 \\\"untrained dt_emb consistently prevents collapse and suppresses v/e,  with recovery dynamics varying across seeds\\\"。 核心 finding（value suppression → no collapse）在 3/3 seeds robust。 V-recovery 作为 secondary pattern 在 2/3 seeds 出现，可作为 suggestive evidence 而非 strong claim。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档假设：008a V-recovery 在 2/3 seeds 出现，1 seed 仅 plateau 不 recover。 Seed 0 已确认双 V-recovery（501→608→470→778）。 Seed 1 预期类似 pattern：untrained dt_emb 抑制 value overestimation， 允许 actor 在过拟合后恢复，但 peak 略低于 seed 0（720 vs 778）。 Seed 2 是 median 档的区分点——normalized v/e 仍被抑制（<1.0x，无 collapse）， 但 eval return 在 530 附近 plateau 而非形成清晰 V-recovery。 可能机制：seed 2 的 actor 收敛到一个 suboptimal 但 stable 的 policy， value suppression 阻止了 overestimation 但 exploration 不足以跳出 local optimum。 关键是 3/3 seeds 都 no collapse + normalized v/e <1.0x， protective effect 是 robust 的；V-recovery 的具体 pattern 有 seed variance。 cross_seed_mean_105K = (778+720+580)/3 ≈ 693，落在 median 档指标范围 [550,720] 内。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\",\n    \"description\": \"dt=1 baseline in second DMC environment, establishing Cheetah-specific v/e calibration\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed0_eval_return_55K\": 450,\n      \"seed0_eval_return_105K\": 680,\n      \"seed0_eval_return_asymptotic\": 780,\n      \"seed1_eval_return_55K\": 430,\n      \"seed1_eval_return_105K\": 660,\n      \"seed1_eval_return_asymptotic\": 760,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_55K\": 470,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_105K\": 700,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_asymptotic\": 800,\n      \"mean_eval_return_asymptotic\": 780,\n      \"mean_value_eval_ratio_35K\": 0.19,\n      \"mean_value_eval_ratio_55K\": 0.35,\n      \"mean_value_eval_ratio_105K\": 0.55,\n      \"ve_stable_range\": \"58-65%\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Cheetah Run baseline v/e calibration (3 seeds)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"step\",\n          \"mean_eval\",\n          \"std_eval\",\n          \"mean_ve\",\n          \"std_ve\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"25K\",\n            220,\n            25,\n            0.1,\n            0.02\n          ],\n          [\n            \"35K\",\n            310,\n            20,\n            0.19,\n            0.03\n          ],\n          [\n            \"55K\",\n            450,\n            20,\n            0.35,\n            0.03\n          ],\n          [\n            \"105K\",\n            680,\n            20,\n            0.55,\n            0.04\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cheetah baseline 的 v/e asymptote 较低（~60% vs Walker ~70%）， 这将影响 normalized v/e 的解读——同样的 absolute v/e 在 Cheetah 中 normalized 更高。 需要 environment-specific calibration，不能直接复用 Walker 的 1.5x 阈值。\\n\\n\\nCheetah Run 的 DreamerV3 baseline 通常低于 Walker Walk（~780 vs ~950）。 Cheetah Run 的 dynamics 更连续平滑（locomotion on flat terrain）， RSSM 对 Cheetah 的 reconstruction quality 通常优于 Walker（接触力学更简单）。 v/e 稳态 58-65% 略低于 Walker 的 69-72%，反映 Cheetah 的 reward landscape 不同。 3 seeds variance 预期 ±3-5%，略高于 Walker（Cheetah 的 reward 更连续 → 更多 local optima）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\",\n    \"description\": \"Replicate delusional critic in Cheetah Run: dt=2 + subsample ON + trained dt_emb + H=8\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed0_eval_return_25K\": 160,\n      \"seed0_eval_return_35K\": 200,\n      \"seed0_eval_return_45K\": 195,\n      \"seed0_eval_return_55K\": 180,\n      \"seed0_normalized_ve_35K\": 1.35,\n      \"seed0_normalized_ve_45K\": 1.45,\n      \"seed0_normalized_ve_55K\": 1.5,\n      \"seed0_verdict\": \"DEGRADATION_BORDERLINE\",\n      \"seed1_eval_return_35K\": 220,\n      \"seed1_eval_return_55K\": 205,\n      \"seed1_normalized_ve_35K\": 1.25,\n      \"seed1_normalized_ve_55K\": 1.38,\n      \"seed1_verdict\": \"DEGRADATION_MILD\",\n      \"seed2_eval_return_35K\": 185,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_55K\": 165,\n      \"seed2_normalized_ve_35K\": 1.4,\n      \"seed2_normalized_ve_55K\": 1.52,\n      \"seed2_verdict\": \"DEGRADATION_BORDERLINE\",\n      \"cross_seed_mean_eval_55K\": 183,\n      \"cheetah_trained_dtEmb_peak_normalized_ve\": 1.35,\n      \"collapse_count\": 0,\n      \"vs_baseline_pct_55K\": \"-59%\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Cheetah trained dt_emb (3 seeds) vs Walker 008d\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"env\",\n          \"step\",\n          \"mean_eval\",\n          \"mean_nve\",\n          \"walker_008d_nve\",\n          \"gap\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Cheetah\",\n            \"25K\",\n            170,\n            1.2,\n            1.78,\n            \"-0.58x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Cheetah\",\n            \"35K\",\n            202,\n            1.33,\n            1.71,\n            \"-0.38x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Cheetah\",\n            \"45K\",\n            195,\n            1.42,\n            2.09,\n            \"-0.67x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Cheetah\",\n            \"55K\",\n            183,\n            1.47,\n            \"N/A (collapsed)\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cheetah 的 trained dt_emb 效果是 \\\"attenuated Walker\\\" 而非 \\\"clean replication\\\"。 这是 median 档的核心挑战：collapse 不复现，但 degradation 和 elevated v/e 复现。 需要 reframe C2：dt_embedding 的危害程度由 RSSM fidelity at dt>1 调节。 Walker 的 contact dynamics → 高 RSSM error → 快速 collapse。 Cheetah 的 smooth dynamics → 低 RSSM error → 慢速 degradation。 v/e overshoot ratio >1.5x 阈值在 Cheetah 中不是硬界限而是 \\\"warning zone\\\"。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心假设：Cheetah Run 中 trained dt_emb 降性能但 collapse 不如 Walker 剧烈 （normalized v/e 1.2-1.5x，边界区）。 机制：Cheetah 的 dynamics 比 Walker 更平滑连续，RSSM 在 dt=2 的 prediction error 较低。 因此 trained dt_emb 导致的 value overestimation 速度更慢、幅度更小。 normalized v/e 在 1.2-1.5x 区间——超过 baseline 但未达到 Walker 的 >2.0x 加速 diverge。 Eval return 呈缓慢下降趋势（200→180）而非 Walker 的急剧 collapse（167→141）。 这产生了关键的 \\\"environment-dependent modulation\\\" 叙事： 相同的 dt_embedding 机制在不同 RSSM fidelity 条件下产生不同严重程度。 从方法论看，这其实 *strengthens* 而非 weakens 因果解释—— 因为它指向 RSSM prediction quality 作为调节变量，与 C2 机制一致。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\",\n    \"description\": \"Causal control in Cheetah: dt=2 + subsample ON + dt_embed_dim=0 + H=8\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed0_eval_return_35K\": 195,\n      \"seed0_eval_return_55K\": 220,\n      \"seed0_normalized_ve_35K\": 0.82,\n      \"seed0_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.75,\n      \"seed1_eval_return_55K\": 210,\n      \"seed1_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.8,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_55K\": 230,\n      \"seed2_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.72,\n      \"cross_seed_mean_eval_55K\": 220,\n      \"cross_seed_mean_nve_55K\": 0.76,\n      \"cheetah_no_dtEmb_normalized_ve\": 0.76,\n      \"vs_baseline_pct_55K\": \"-51%\",\n      \"vs_trained_dtEmb_gap_eval\": \"+37 (220 vs 183)\",\n      \"vs_trained_dtEmb_gap_nve\": \"-0.71x (0.76 vs 1.47)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Cheetah 008f-equivalent vs trained dt_emb (mean across 3 seeds)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"config\",\n          \"eval_55K\",\n          \"nve_55K\",\n          \"collapse\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"trained dt_emb\",\n            183,\n            1.47,\n            \"degradation (no collapse)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"dt_embed_dim=0\",\n            220,\n            0.76,\n            \"no degradation\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"baseline\",\n            450,\n            \"1.0 (reference)\",\n            \"N/A\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"因果方向在 Cheetah 仍成立（removing dt_emb → lower v/e + better performance）， 但 effect size 是 Walker 的约 50%。这是论文中 \\\"boundary conditions\\\" section 的核心数据： 当 RSSM prediction quality 较好时（Cheetah），dt_embedding 的危害减轻但不消失。 cheetah_no_dtEmb_normalized_ve=0.76 落在 median 档指标范围 [0.7, 1.15] 内。\\n\\n\\n移除 dt_embedding 在 Cheetah 中同样消除 elevated v/e，但 performance gap 较 Walker 小。 在 Walker 中，008f vs 008d 的 eval gap 明显（207 vs 141@55K）。 在 Cheetah 中，gap 缩小（220 vs 183@55K），因为 baseline degradation 本身较温和。 Normalized v/e 在 0.7-1.15x 范围（median 档指标），低于 1.0x 表示 no overestimation。 因果方向仍一致（有 dt_emb → nve>1.2x, 无 dt_emb → nve<1.0x），但 effect size 较小。 这支持 \\\"dt_embedding is harmful but severity is environment-modulated\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\",\n    \"description\": \"Value growth suppression in Cheetah: dt=2 + subsample OFF + untrained dt_emb + H=15\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed0_eval_return_55K\": 380,\n      \"seed0_eval_return_105K\": 550,\n      \"seed0_normalized_ve_105K\": 0.72,\n      \"seed1_eval_return_105K\": 520,\n      \"seed1_normalized_ve_105K\": 0.78,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_105K\": 490,\n      \"seed2_normalized_ve_105K\": 0.82,\n      \"cross_seed_mean_105K\": 520,\n      \"vs_baseline_pct_105K\": \"-24%\",\n      \"v_recovery_count\": \"1/3 seeds shows V-recovery, 2/3 plateau\",\n      \"cheetah_best_dt2_vs_baseline_pct\": \"67%\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Cheetah untrained dt_emb recovery (3 seeds)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"step\",\n          \"seed0\",\n          \"seed1\",\n          \"seed2\",\n          \"mean\",\n          \"nve_mean\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"55K\",\n            380,\n            360,\n            350,\n            363,\n            0.88\n          ],\n          [\n            \"75K\",\n            420,\n            440,\n            410,\n            423,\n            0.82\n          ],\n          [\n            \"105K\",\n            550,\n            520,\n            490,\n            520,\n            0.77\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cheetah 的 untrained dt_emb configuration 确认 protective effect（no collapse, nve<1.0x） 但 recovery 更缓慢。这与 environment-dependent modulation 假设一致： Cheetah 的 RSSM error 较低 → dt_emb 的影响（有害或保护性的）都被 attenuate。 论文中可用此数据支持 \\\"the dt_embedding mechanism is general,  but its magnitude scales with RSSM prediction error\\\"。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档假设：Cheetah 中 untrained dt_emb 有保护作用但 gap 较小。 Walker 中 008a 达 baseline 85%（778/916），Cheetah 预期只达 67%（520/780）。 原因：Cheetah 的 smooth dynamics 使 RSSM error 较低 → trained dt_emb 的危害本就较小 →  untrained dt_emb 的 \\\"保护效果\\\" 相对 margin 也较小（从 183 到 220 vs 从 141 到 207 in Walker）。 V-recovery pattern 在 Cheetah 中更弱：只有 1/3 seeds 出现， 因为 Cheetah 的 reward landscape 更平 → actor 倾向 plateau 而非 oscillate。 cheetah_best_dt2_vs_baseline_pct=67% 落在 median 档指标范围 [50%, 75%] 内。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\",\n    \"description\": \"Measure observation/reward reconstruction loss at dt=2 vs dt=1 from existing trained models across both environments\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"walker_rssm_recon_loss_dt1\": 4.2,\n      \"walker_rssm_recon_loss_dt2\": 6.8,\n      \"walker_dt2_dt1_ratio\": 1.62,\n      \"cheetah_rssm_recon_loss_dt1\": 3.9,\n      \"cheetah_rssm_recon_loss_dt2\": 5.1,\n      \"cheetah_dt2_dt1_ratio\": 1.31,\n      \"walker_reward_pred_error_dt1\": 0.08,\n      \"walker_reward_pred_error_dt2\": 0.25,\n      \"cheetah_reward_pred_error_dt1\": 0.06,\n      \"cheetah_reward_pred_error_dt2\": 0.12,\n      \"cross_env_recon_gap_ratio\": 1.24\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"RSSM reconstruction loss: dt=1 vs dt=2 × environment\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"environment\",\n          \"loss_dt1\",\n          \"loss_dt2\",\n          \"ratio\",\n          \"reward_err_dt1\",\n          \"reward_err_dt2\",\n          \"reward_ratio\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Walker Walk\",\n            4.2,\n            6.8,\n            1.62,\n            0.08,\n            0.25,\n            3.13\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Cheetah Run\",\n            3.9,\n            5.1,\n            1.31,\n            0.06,\n            0.12,\n            2.0\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"plan_030 提供了 \\\"environment-dependent modulation\\\" 假设的 mechanistic foundation。 Walker 的 RSSM dt2/dt1 gap 比 Cheetah 大 ~24%（1.62/1.31=1.24x）， 这与 Walker 中 trained dt_emb 导致更严重 collapse 的观察一致。 但只有两个环境点，无法建立 quantitative 关系。 论文中应呈现为 \\\"consistent with the hypothesis\\\" 而非 \\\"proves\\\"。 如果 plan_040（Hopper Hop）执行，将提供第三个点。\\n\\n\\n这是 median 档叙事的关键支撑实验——直接量化 RSSM fidelity gap 的 environment dependence。 Walker Walk 涉及 contact dynamics（脚与地面碰撞），dt=2 跳过一个接触事件时 RSSM 需要 \\\"想象\\\" 中间状态，reconstruction loss 预期升高 ~60%（ratio 1.6x）。 Cheetah Run 的 dynamics 更平滑（无离散接触切换）， dt=2 的 prediction 误差增幅较小（~30%, ratio 1.3x）。 这个 1.6x vs 1.3x 的差距直接解释了为什么 trained dt_emb 在 Walker 导致 collapse  而在 Cheetah 仅导致 degradation：更大的 RSSM error → 更多 delusional critic gradient → 更快 collapse。 Reward prediction error 的环境间差异更大（3.1x vs 2.0x ratio）， 因为 Walker 的 reward 与接触事件强耦合。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Actor entropy analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Plot actor entropy vs training step for healthy (008a/008c/008f) vs collapsed (006/008d) configurations\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"walker_008d_entropy_25K\": 3.8,\n      \"walker_008d_entropy_35K\": 4.1,\n      \"walker_008d_entropy_45K\": 4.5,\n      \"walker_008d_entropy_trend\": \"increasing\",\n      \"walker_006_entropy_35K\": 3.9,\n      \"walker_006_entropy_55K\": 5.2,\n      \"walker_006_entropy_trend\": \"sharply_increasing\",\n      \"walker_008a_entropy_55K\": 3.2,\n      \"walker_008a_entropy_105K\": 2.8,\n      \"walker_008a_entropy_trend\": \"stable_to_decreasing\",\n      \"walker_008f_entropy_35K\": 3.5,\n      \"walker_008f_entropy_trend\": \"stable\",\n      \"walker_baseline_entropy_35K\": 3.0,\n      \"walker_baseline_entropy_105K\": 2.5,\n      \"walker_baseline_entropy_trend\": \"decreasing\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Actor entropy trajectories\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"config\",\n          \"entropy_25K\",\n          \"entropy_35K\",\n          \"entropy_45K\",\n          \"entropy_55K\",\n          \"trend\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"baseline\",\n            3.2,\n            3.0,\n            2.9,\n            2.8,\n            \"decreasing\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"008d (collapse)\",\n            3.8,\n            4.1,\n            4.5,\n            \"—\",\n            \"increasing\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"006 (collapse)\",\n            3.5,\n            3.9,\n            4.2,\n            5.2,\n            \"sharply increasing\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"008a (V-recovery)\",\n            3.3,\n            3.1,\n            3.0,\n            3.2,\n            \"stable\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"008f (stable)\",\n            3.4,\n            3.5,\n            3.3,\n            \"—\",\n            \"stable\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Entropy analysis 为 C2 提供 corroborating evidence 而非 primary evidence。 Collapsed configs 的 entropy 上升模式与 \\\"delusional critic → actor confusion\\\" 一致。 在 paper 中作为 supplementary figure 或 appendix，支撑 main text 的 causal diagram。\\n\\n\\nActor entropy 增高表示 policy 变得更随机——这是 delusional critic gradient 的下游症状。 当 value function 高估 → actor 收到 misleading gradient → policy 不再有 clear preference → entropy 升高。 预期 collapsed configs（008d, 006）显示 entropy 单调上升（actor confusion）， 而 healthy configs（008a, 008f, baseline）显示 entropy stable 或下降（policy sharpening）。 这不是新发现，但提供了 mechanism 的额外 sanity check： 如果 collapsed configs 的 entropy *不*上升，则 C2 的 \\\"delusional critic → actor degradation\\\" 链需要修正。 Median 档下预期 pattern 清晰但 noise 较大（因为 entropy 是 high-variance metric）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\",\n    \"description\": \"Distribution plots of V(s) vs Monte Carlo return for trained vs untrained dt_emb\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"walker_008d_value_mc_correlation\": 0.35,\n      \"walker_008d_value_bias\": \"+45% (systematic overestimation)\",\n      \"walker_008d_value_std_ratio\": 2.1,\n      \"walker_008a_value_mc_correlation\": 0.72,\n      \"walker_008a_value_bias\": \"+8% (mild overestimation)\",\n      \"walker_008a_value_std_ratio\": 1.2,\n      \"walker_baseline_value_mc_correlation\": 0.85,\n      \"walker_baseline_value_bias\": \"+5%\",\n      \"walker_baseline_value_std_ratio\": 1.1,\n      \"walker_008f_value_mc_correlation\": 0.68,\n      \"walker_008f_value_bias\": \"+10%\",\n      \"walker_008f_value_std_ratio\": 1.3\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Value calibration summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"config\",\n          \"correlation\",\n          \"bias_pct\",\n          \"variance_ratio\",\n          \"verdict\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"baseline\",\n            0.85,\n            \"+5%\",\n            1.1,\n            \"calibrated\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"008a (untrained)\",\n            0.72,\n            \"+8%\",\n            1.2,\n            \"mildly_optimistic\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"008f (no dt_emb)\",\n            0.68,\n            \"+10%\",\n            1.3,\n            \"mildly_optimistic\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"008d (trained)\",\n            0.35,\n            \"+45%\",\n            2.1,\n            \"delusional\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Distribution analysis 将 v/e ratio proxy 升级为更 rigorous 的 value calibration 证据。 008d 的 correlation=0.35 和 bias=+45% 直接证明 \\\"delusional\\\"——value function 的预测 与实际 return 几乎 decouple 且系统性偏高。 这是 paper 中最强的 supplementary evidence，值得在 main text 中给一段或一个 figure。\\n\\n\\nV(s) vs MC return 的联合分布揭示 v/e ratio 无法捕捉的细节。 008d（trained dt_emb, collapse）预期显示：(a) systematic positive bias（值线远高于 y=x）， (b) 低相关性（value 与实际 return decouple），(c) 高 variance ratio（value 在不确定状态大幅波动）。 这三个特征共同构成 \\\"delusional critic\\\" 的 distributional fingerprint。 008a/008f（healthy configs）预期接近 baseline 分布，bias 小、相关性高。 Median 档下预期 pattern 清晰但 008f 的 correlation 略低于 baseline （因为 dt=2 imagination 本身引入了一些 noise，即使没有 dt_embedding）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Analyze learned dt_embedding vectors: cosine similarity between dt=1 and dt=2\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"cosine_sim_5K\": 0.92,\n      \"cosine_sim_15K\": 0.75,\n      \"cosine_sim_35K\": 0.42,\n      \"cosine_sim_55K\": 0.28,\n      \"embedding_norm_dt1_35K\": 1.2,\n      \"embedding_norm_dt2_35K\": 2.8,\n      \"embedding_divergence_onset\": \"~15K-25K (coincides with v/e acceleration)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"dt_embedding evolution during training\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"step\",\n          \"cosine_sim\",\n          \"norm_dt1\",\n          \"norm_dt2\",\n          \"nve_at_step\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"5K\",\n            0.92,\n            0.8,\n            0.9,\n            \"~1.0x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"15K\",\n            0.75,\n            1.0,\n            1.4,\n            \"~1.2x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"25K\",\n            0.55,\n            1.1,\n            2.1,\n            \"~1.5x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"35K\",\n            0.42,\n            1.2,\n            2.8,\n            \"~1.7x\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cosine similarity 分析提供 mechanistic timeline：embedding 分离 → value exploitation → collapse。 这是 P2 priority 因为它补充而非替代 core evidence， 但在论文中可以做一个很有说服力的 timeline figure。 如果 embedding 的分离时间与 v/e 加速不吻合，则 C2 的 mechanism story 需要修正。\\n\\n\\nTrained dt_embedding 在训练过程中逐步学会区分 dt=1 和 dt=2。 早期（<10K）dt=1 和 dt=2 embedding 相似（cosine~0.9），value function 尚未 exploit 差异。 15-25K 时 embedding 开始分离（cosine 下降到 0.5-0.7）， 这恰好与 v/e ratio 开始加速的时间窗口吻合。 这提供了 temporal evidence：dt_embedding 的学习 → value function 开始 exploit → overestimation → collapse。 dt=2 embedding 的 norm 增大（2.8 vs dt=1 的 1.2）表明 value function 放大了 dt=2 的表征， 可能因为 dt=2 transition 在 imagination 中产生更大的 \\\"value opportunity\\\"（但实际是虚假的）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\",\n    \"description\": \"Third DMC environment: baseline + trained dt_emb + dt_embed_dim=0\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"baseline_asymptotic\": 250,\n      \"trained_dtEmb_peak\": 120,\n      \"trained_dtEmb_nve_peak\": 1.55,\n      \"trained_dtEmb_collapse\": \"partial (1/3 seeds collapse, 2/3 degradation)\",\n      \"no_dtEmb_eval_55K\": 105,\n      \"no_dtEmb_nve_55K\": 0.85,\n      \"baseline_ve_stable\": \"55-62%\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Hopper Hop results summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"config\",\n          \"mean_eval_55K\",\n          \"mean_nve_55K\",\n          \"collapse_fraction\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"baseline\",\n            180,\n            \"1.0 (ref)\",\n            \"0/3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"trained dt_emb\",\n            95,\n            1.55,\n            \"1/3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"dt_embed_dim=0\",\n            105,\n            0.85,\n            \"0/3\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Hopper 作为第三环境，主要贡献是验证 environment-dependent modulation 假设。 如果 RSSM dt2/dt1 ratio 介于 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间（如 plan_030 预测）， 且 normalized v/e 也介于两者之间，则三个点落在一条正相关趋势线上—— 这将 \\\"environment-dependent modulation\\\" 从 post-hoc 假设升级为 empirical pattern。 但 P2 priority 意味着在 CoRL deadline 前可能无法完成。 Median 档论文即使没有 Hopper 也可以成立，用 Discussion 中的 \\\"boundary conditions\\\" 段覆盖。\\n\\nHopper Hop 是高难度 DMC task（baseline ~250 远低于 Walker ~950 和 Cheetah ~780）。 RSSM prediction quality 介于 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间 （有 hopping contact events 但比 walking 更规律）。 Median 档下预期 trained dt_emb 的 normalized v/e 在 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间（~1.5x）， 1/3 seeds collapse，2/3 degradation。 dt_embed_dim=0 仍应 stable（nve <1.0x）。 但 Hopper 的 absolute performance 很低，signal-to-noise ratio 差 →  结论 less conclusive，主要价值是提供 plan_030 scatter plot 的第三个点。 P2 priority，论文如时间不够可省略。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":836,"startLine":1,"totalLines":836}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DiFxAnxst7V5TscVeMmE24","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HWuKsJpHZnhSViecf3KMjB","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_9/projects/event-gated-adaptive-horizon/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T062606/median/paper_framing.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11628,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11628},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e39ae06-ebff-4a82-a634-fdad224fbc5c","uuid":"f8c2c2b8-488c-4c9d-8798-f6bdd0d9d9be"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HWuKsJpHZnhSViecf3KMjB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing: Diagnostic Analysis of Temporal Abstraction in World-Model RL\n2\t\n3\t## Title Candidates\n4\t\n5\t1. **\"Why Temporal Abstraction Fails in World-Model Reinforcement Learning: A Diagnostic Analysis\"**\n6\t2. **\"The Delusional Critic Problem in Variable-Rate Imagination\"**\n7\t3. **\"Diagnosing Value Overestimation in Temporally-Abstract World Models\"**\n8\t\n9\t## Venue\n10\t\n11\t**CoRL 2026** — Deadline: 2026-05-29\n12\t\n13\t## Narrative Positioning\n14\t\n15\tThis is a **diagnostic analysis paper**, not a method paper. We do not propose a new algorithm. Instead, we provide a systematic, controlled investigation answering: *Why does temporal abstraction fail in world-model RL?*\n16\t\n17\tThe contribution is a **closed causal chain** from mechanism to failure mode, backed by a factorial experiment design that isolates each factor. Diagnostic papers are valued when they (a) address a widely-attempted but poorly-understood failure, (b) provide actionable insight for future method design, and (c) are methodologically rigorous.\n18\t\n19\t---\n20\t\n21\t## Core Claims\n22\t\n23\t### C1: Variable-rate imagination in DreamerV3 consistently degrades performance\n24\t\n25\tTemporal abstraction via variable dt—whether learned or fixed—degrades asymptotic performance relative to the dt=1 baseline across all tested configurations.\n26\t\n27\t| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n28\t|----------|-----------|------------|\n29\t| Baseline stability | exp_001_baseline (dt=1) | Stable convergence ~950 eval return |\n30\t| Fixed dt=2 collapse | exp_006_fixed_dt2 (dt=2, subsample ON, H=15) | Peak 485@35K → collapse to ~135@65K |\n31\t| Fixed dt=4 severe degradation | exp_007_fixed_dt4 (dt=4) | Peak 176.9@25K, 144.4@45K (33% of baseline@45K=443) |\n32\t| Learned gate collapse | exp_005 (learned gate) | Peak 541@55K → 99@145K |\n33\t\n34\t**Strength**: Strong. Three independent dt>1 configurations all show degradation. No positive result exists for variable-rate imagination in our setup.\n35\t\n36\t### C2: Trained dt_embedding causes delusional critic (root cause)\n37\t\n38\t**⚠️ Causal attribution pending**: Current 008c vs 008d comparison confounds dt_embedding training with RSSM training data composition (subsample ON/OFF). exp_008f (dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON + dt=2 imagination + H=8) will isolate the dt_embedding variable. C2 strength is provisional until 008f completes.\n39\t\n40\tThe trained dt_embedding enables precise dt prediction in imagination, but RSSM state prediction quality at dt>1 is insufficient to support this precision. The result is systematic value overestimation (delusional critic) that drives actor learning toward incorrect policies.\n41\t\n42\t| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n43\t|----------|-----------|------------|\n44\t| Untrained dt_emb, no collapse | exp_008c (dt=2, subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=8) | eval plateau ~242@55K; v/e: @35K=21.8% (0.90x) → @55K=29.1% (0.72x) → @65K=32.8% (0.58x) (declining normalized v/e, ~7x slower than trained) |\n45\t| Trained dt_emb, collapse | exp_008d (dt=2, subsample ON, trained dt_emb, H=8) | eval declining 167→146→141 @25K→35K→45K; v/e: @25K=15.5% (1.78x) → @35K=41.2% (1.71x) → @45K=69.3% (2.09x) (accelerating overestimation) |\n46\t| Both trained dt_emb → accelerating v/e | exp_006 (H=15) vs exp_008d (H=8) | 006: v/e @35K=31.1% (1.29x)→@45K=53.3% (1.61x)→@55K=93.3% (2.31x); 008d: v/e @35K=41.2% (1.71x)→@45K=69.3% (2.09x) — both show accelerating normalized v/e leading to collapse |\n47\t| Baseline v/e calibration (overshoot reference) | exp_001_baseline | v/e@35K=24.1%, @45K=33.1%, @55K=40.4%. Overshoot ratio: 008d@35K=1.7x, @45K=2.1x; 006@45K=1.6x, @55K=2.3x (all >1.5x = pathological) |\n48\t\n49\t**Strength**: Strong. The 008c vs 008d comparison is a controlled experiment isolating dt_embedding training as the single variable. The v/e overshoot ratio (experiment v/e / baseline v/e at same step) quantitatively identifies pathological regimes: trained dt_emb variants exceed 1.5x baseline before collapse, while untrained variants stay at or below baseline levels. **Pending confirmation**: exp_008f (dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON) will isolate whether dt_embedding conditioning or RSSM's learned dt=2 dynamics is the true cause.\n50\t\n51\t### C3: Untrained dt_embedding prevents optimistic drift, substantively protecting performance\n52\t\n53\tWhen dt_embedding is untrained (random fixed), the value function cannot exploit precise dt information, preventing the optimistic value drift seen in trained variants. This value growth suppression substantively protects performance: exp_008a demonstrates two complete V-shaped recovery cycles over 105K steps (peak @105K=778, 85% of baseline 916), with normalized v/e consistently suppressed at 0.59-0.93x baseline. The trained dt_embedding variant (exp_006) collapses catastrophically as its v/e ratio accelerates far past baseline levels (2.3x baseline@55K).\n54\t\n55\t| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n56\t|----------|-----------|------------|\n57\t| Two V-shaped recoveries (105K) | exp_008a (dt=2, subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=15) | 501→563→488→608→470→584→572→778; two complete recovery cycles over 105K steps. @65K=608 (-1.3% baseline), @105K=778 (-15.1% baseline, 85% of 916). No collapse. |\n58\t| Sustained v/e suppression | exp_008a | v/e: 37.6%@55K → 37.2%@65K → 53.6%@75K → 47.5%@85K → 49.7%@95K → 38.6%@105K. Normalized v/e: 0.93x→0.66x→0.75x→0.68x→0.79x→0.59x baseline. Consistently below 1.0x, no acceleration. |\n59\t| Trained dt_emb: accelerating collapse | exp_006 (dt=2, subsample ON, trained dt_emb, H=15) | 485→477→360→collapse; v/e: 53.3%@45K (1.61x)→93.3%@55K (2.31x) → immediate collapse |\n60\t| v/e rate comparison (H=8 controlled) | exp_008c vs exp_008d | 008c (untrained): @35K=21.8% (0.90x)→@65K=32.8% (0.58x) (normalized declining); 008d (trained): @25K=15.5% (1.78x)→@35K=41.2% (1.71x) (normalized >1.5x = pathological). ~7x slower overestimation rate |\n61\t| Baseline v/e calibration | exp_001_baseline | v/e: 8.7%@25K → 24.1%@35K → 40.4%@55K → 56.3%@65K → 65.6%@105K (stable 69-72% from 135K+). 008a normalized v/e: 0.93x@55K → 0.66x@65K → 0.59x@105K (suppressed, diverging further below baseline); 008d: 1.7x@35K → 2.1x@45K (optimistic drift) |\n62\t\n63\t**Strength**: Strong (B+ confirmed with 105K long-run data). Two complete V-shaped recovery cycles (501→608→470→778) with normalized v/e consistently 0.59-0.93x baseline across 105K steps. This is structural value growth suppression, not a transient delay. Contrasts sharply with exp_006's accelerating v/e (1.6x→2.3x baseline → collapse). The mechanism is clear: untrained dt_embedding prevents the value function from exploiting precise (but wrong) dt>1 predictions, suppressing the optimistic value drift that drives the delusional critic feedback loop in trained variants.\n64\t\n65\t**Diagnostic metric: v/e overshoot ratio** = experiment v/e / baseline v/e at same training step. >1.5x = pathological warning. Trained dt_emb variants: 008d@35K=1.7x, @45K=2.1x; 006@45K=1.6x, @55K=2.3x. Untrained: 008a normalized v/e range 0.59-0.93x over 55K-105K (consistently below baseline = healthy, diverging further from baseline over time).\n66\t\n67\t**105K long-run confirmed**: exp_008a ran to 112K steps. Normalized v/e at 105K=0.59x baseline (lowest point), confirming value growth suppression is structural, not a transient delay. The suppression strengthens over time rather than converging to baseline levels.\n68\t\n69\t### C4: Longer dt amplifies the problem\n70\t\n71\tIncreasing dt from 2 to 4 worsens degradation, consistent with RSSM prediction error compounding over longer temporal gaps.\n72\t\n73\t| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n74\t|----------|-----------|------------|\n75\t| dt=2 degradation | exp_006_fixed_dt2 | Peak 485, collapse to ~135 |\n76\t| dt=4 severe degradation | exp_007_fixed_dt4 | Peak 176.9@25K, 144.4@45K (33% of baseline@45K=443) |\n77\t| Monotonic relationship | dt=1 (~950) > dt=2 (peak 485@35K) > dt=4 (peak 177@25K) | Clear monotonic decline |\n78\t\n79\t**Strength**: Moderate. Only two dt values tested (2 and 4). The monotonic trend is clear but a finer grid (dt=3, dt=6) would strengthen this claim. Sufficient for a supporting claim but not a standalone finding.\n80\t\n81\t### C5: Learning signal reduction from shorter effective horizons compounds degradation but is not the root cause\n82\t\n83\tSubsampling with dt>1 reduces the effective number of learning transitions per episode. This contributes to degradation but is neither necessary nor sufficient for collapse.\n84\t\n85\t| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n86\t|----------|-----------|------------|\n87\t| Subsample OFF, still degraded | exp_008c (subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=8) | eval ~242 vs baseline ~950 |\n88\t| Subsample OFF, no collapse | exp_008a (subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=15) | eval 778@105K (85% baseline), no collapse through 112K steps |\n89\t| Subsample ON, collapse | exp_008d (subsample ON, trained dt_emb, H=8) | eval 146, value overestimation |\n90\t| Horizon effect | exp_008c (H=8) vs exp_008a (H=15) | H=15 significantly outperforms H=8, both subsample OFF |\n91\t\n92\t**Strength**: Moderate. The 008c vs 008a comparison shows horizon length matters independently. But disentangling horizon from subsample effects requires additional controls. The key point—that it's not the root cause—is well-supported by 008c's stability despite lower performance.\n93\t\n94\t---\n95\t\n96\t## Story Arc\n97\t\n98\t### 1. Introduction\n99\t- Temporal abstraction is a long-sought goal in RL (options, macro-actions, skip connections)\n100\t- World-model RL (DreamerV3) offers a natural testbed: modify imagination dt without changing environment interaction\n101\t- Puzzle: all our attempts at variable-rate imagination degrade performance. Why?\n102\t- Contribution: systematic factorial diagnosis identifying trained dt_embedding → delusional critic as the root cause\n103\t\n104\t### 2. Background & Related Work\n105\t- Temporal abstraction in model-free RL (options framework, FiGAR, action repeat)\n106\t- World-model RL (Dreamer family, IRIS, TWM)\n107\t- Variable-rate planning in world models (few prior works, mostly positive framing)\n108\t- Value overestimation / delusional policies in model-based RL\n109\t\n110\t### 3. Methodology\n111\t- DreamerV3 as base architecture\n112\t- Variable-rate imagination: dt_embedding, temporal subsampling, learned gating\n113\t- **Factorial experiment design**: 2×2×2 grid (dt_embedding trained/untrained × subsample ON/OFF × H=8/15) + baselines\n114\t- Diagnostic metrics: eval return, value/eval ratio as overestimation proxy, learning curves\n115\t\n116\t### 4. Results\n117\t- **Finding 1**: All dt>1 configurations degrade (C1)\n118\t- **Finding 2**: Controlled ablation isolates trained dt_embedding (C2) — the \"smoking gun\" comparison (008c vs 008d)\n119\t- **Finding 3**: Untrained dt_embedding prevents optimistic drift, sustaining near-baseline performance (C3)\n120\t- **Finding 4**: Longer dt amplifies (C4)\n121\t- **Finding 5**: Horizon/subsample effects are secondary (C5)\n122\t\n123\t### 5. Discussion\n124\t- Mechanism: why trained dt_embedding causes delusional critic (RSSM fidelity gap at dt>1)\n125\t- Connection to existing theory: delusional policies (Delalleau et al.), model exploitation in MBRL\n126\t- Why this is specific to world-model RL (model-free temporal abstraction doesn't suffer the same failure mode)\n127\t\n128\t### 6. Implications for Future Work\n129\t- Don't train dt_embedding jointly with value function in current world-model architectures\n130\t- RSSM prediction quality must improve before variable-rate imagination is viable\n131\t- Value growth suppression (e.g., untrained dt_embedding) as a potential mitigation direction\n132\t- Need for diagnostic methodology in temporal abstraction research\n133\t\n134\t---\n135\t\n136\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n137\t\n138\t### R1: \"Limited to one environment / one base algorithm\"\n139\t**Pre-emption**: Our claims are mechanistic (trained dt_embedding → value overestimation → collapse). The causal chain is architecture-specific by design—we diagnose *why* it fails in DreamerV3, not whether it fails everywhere. The mechanism (RSSM fidelity gap) likely generalizes to other latent-dynamics models but we scope claims conservatively.\n140\t**Mitigation**: Cheetah Run is a planned experiment in our experiment schedule, not a stretch goal. We will include at least one additional DMC environment (Cheetah Run) to demonstrate generality of the mechanism.\n141\t\n142\t### R2: \"No proposed solution — what's the actionable takeaway?\"\n143\t**Pre-emption**: Diagnostic papers serve a different purpose than method papers. Identifying root causes (trained dt_embedding) and quantitative signatures (v/e overshoot ratio >1.5x baseline = pathological) gives the community concrete guidance. We explicitly outline mitigation directions (value growth suppression, improved RSSM, decoupled dt_embedding training).\n144\t**Mitigation**: Frame implications section as a \"research agenda\" with specific, testable hypotheses.\n145\t\n146\t### R3: \"Value/eval ratio is a crude proxy for overestimation\"\n147\t**Pre-emption**: We acknowledge this is a proxy, not a formal divergence measure. However, the v/e overshoot ratio (experiment v/e / baseline v/e at same step) consistently identifies pathological overestimation: trained dt_emb variants exceed 1.5x baseline v/e before collapse, while untrained variants stay at or below baseline levels.\n148\t**Mitigation**: Add distributional analysis of value predictions vs. realized returns if time permits.\n149\t\n150\t### R4: \"The factorial design is incomplete — missing cells in the grid\"\n151\t**Pre-emption**: We prioritized the most informative comparisons. The 008c vs 008d pair isolates dt_embedding training with all else held constant—this is the critical controlled experiment.\n152\t**Mitigation**: Explicitly present the factorial grid, mark which cells are filled, and justify the prioritization.\n153\t\n154\t### R5: \"Novelty concern — model exploitation / value overestimation in MBRL is well-known\"\n155\t**Pre-emption**: General MBRL overestimation is known (Janner et al., 2019), but the specific mechanism through temporal abstraction's dt_embedding is novel. Prior work on temporal abstraction in world models has not identified this failure mode. Our contribution is the *specific causal link*, not the general phenomenon.\n156\t\n157\t### R6: \"All results from a single seed — how robust are the conclusions?\"\n158\t**Pre-emption**: Our claims are about *mechanisms* (causal chain from dt_embedding → value overestimation → collapse), not about precise numerical thresholds. The mechanism manifests consistently across all configurations (exp_005, 006, 007, 008d) — four independent experiments all show the same value/eval ratio divergence pattern. The probability of this pattern appearing by chance across 4 experiments is negligible.\n159\t**Mitigation**: Planned multi-seed runs for final paper. The factorial design (008c vs 008d) provides cross-experiment replication of the core mechanism.\n160\t\n161\t### R7: \"The factorial design confounds dt_embedding training with training data composition\"\n162\t**Pre-emption**: We acknowledge this confound between 008c (subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb) and 008d (subsample ON, trained dt_emb). Experiment 008f (dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON) is designed to resolve this: it trains with dt=2 transitions (like 008d) but without dt_embedding conditioning. If 008f collapses → the cause is RSSM's learned dt=2 dynamics, not dt_embedding per se. If 008f remains stable → dt_embedding conditioning is confirmed as the root cause.\n163\t**Mitigation**: exp_008f is a blocking experiment for the final paper. Results will be available before submission.\n164\t\n165\t---\n166\t\n167\t## Experiment Coverage Assessment\n168\t\n169\t| Claim | Evidence Status | Gaps |\n170\t|-------|----------------|------|\n171\t| C1 (degradation) | ✅ Strong — 3 configurations (005, 006, 007) all negative | Could add 1 more environment |\n172\t| C2 (root cause: dt_emb) | ⚠️ Provisional — pending exp_008f to resolve dt_embedding vs training data confound | Consider adding value prediction distribution analysis |\n173\t| C3 (preventing optimistic drift) | ✅ Strong (105K confirmed) — 008a@105K=778 (85% baseline), normalized v/e=0.59x, two V-shaped recoveries | None — long-term structural suppression confirmed |\n174\t| C4 (dt amplification) | ⚠️ Moderate — only dt=2 vs dt=4 | Would benefit from dt=3, but not blocking |\n175\t| C5 (horizon/subsample) | ⚠️ Moderate — confounded with other factors | Need 008c-equivalent with H=15 + subsample ON + untrained dt_emb for clean isolation |\n176\t\n177\t### Priority Actions Before Submission\n178\t1. ~~**Check exp_008a@65K**~~ — ✅ Done: 608 (-1.3% baseline), B+ confirmed\n179\t2. **Complete factorial grid analysis** — present all 8 cells, even if some are interpolated\n180\t3. **Value prediction distribution plots** — strengthen C2 beyond ratio proxy\n181\t4. **Second environment** (stretch goal) — addresses R1\n182\t\n183\t---\n184\t\n185\t## Key Figures (Planned)\n186\t\n187\t1. **Figure 1**: Learning curves — all experiments overlaid, showing degradation pattern (hero figure)\n188\t2. **Figure 2**: Value/eval ratio over training — separating healthy vs. pathological regimes\n189\t3. **Figure 3**: Factorial grid summary — 2×2 (dt_emb × subsample) with H as secondary axis\n190\t4. **Figure 4**: Causal diagram — dt_embedding → value overestimation → actor degradation → collapse\n191\t5. **Figure 5**: dt=1 vs dt=2 vs dt=4 comparison — monotonic degradation (C4)\n192\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e39ae06-ebff-4a82-a634-fdad224fbc5c","uuid":"acd750fc-7443-4aa4-a0c7-9d30120776fb","timestamp":"2026-05-14T06:46:34.777Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_9/projects/event-gated-adaptive-horizon/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T062606/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing: Diagnostic Analysis of Temporal Abstraction in World-Model RL\n\n## Title Candidates\n\n1. **\"Why Temporal Abstraction Fails in World-Model Reinforcement Learning: A Diagnostic Analysis\"**\n2. **\"The Delusional Critic Problem in Variable-Rate Imagination\"**\n3. **\"Diagnosing Value Overestimation in Temporally-Abstract World Models\"**\n\n## Venue\n\n**CoRL 2026** — Deadline: 2026-05-29\n\n## Narrative Positioning\n\nThis is a **diagnostic analysis paper**, not a method paper. We do not propose a new algorithm. Instead, we provide a systematic, controlled investigation answering: *Why does temporal abstraction fail in world-model RL?*\n\nThe contribution is a **closed causal chain** from mechanism to failure mode, backed by a factorial experiment design that isolates each factor. Diagnostic papers are valued when they (a) address a widely-attempted but poorly-understood failure, (b) provide actionable insight for future method design, and (c) are methodologically rigorous.\n\n---\n\n## Core Claims\n\n### C1: Variable-rate imagination in DreamerV3 consistently degrades performance\n\nTemporal abstraction via variable dt—whether learned or fixed—degrades asymptotic performance relative to the dt=1 baseline across all tested configurations.\n\n| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n|----------|-----------|------------|\n| Baseline stability | exp_001_baseline (dt=1) | Stable convergence ~950 eval return |\n| Fixed dt=2 collapse | exp_006_fixed_dt2 (dt=2, subsample ON, H=15) | Peak 485@35K → collapse to ~135@65K |\n| Fixed dt=4 severe degradation | exp_007_fixed_dt4 (dt=4) | Peak 176.9@25K, 144.4@45K (33% of baseline@45K=443) |\n| Learned gate collapse | exp_005 (learned gate) | Peak 541@55K → 99@145K |\n\n**Strength**: Strong. Three independent dt>1 configurations all show degradation. No positive result exists for variable-rate imagination in our setup.\n\n### C2: Trained dt_embedding causes delusional critic (root cause)\n\n**⚠️ Causal attribution pending**: Current 008c vs 008d comparison confounds dt_embedding training with RSSM training data composition (subsample ON/OFF). exp_008f (dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON + dt=2 imagination + H=8) will isolate the dt_embedding variable. C2 strength is provisional until 008f completes.\n\nThe trained dt_embedding enables precise dt prediction in imagination, but RSSM state prediction quality at dt>1 is insufficient to support this precision. The result is systematic value overestimation (delusional critic) that drives actor learning toward incorrect policies.\n\n| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n|----------|-----------|------------|\n| Untrained dt_emb, no collapse | exp_008c (dt=2, subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=8) | eval plateau ~242@55K; v/e: @35K=21.8% (0.90x) → @55K=29.1% (0.72x) → @65K=32.8% (0.58x) (declining normalized v/e, ~7x slower than trained) |\n| Trained dt_emb, collapse | exp_008d (dt=2, subsample ON, trained dt_emb, H=8) | eval declining 167→146→141 @25K→35K→45K; v/e: @25K=15.5% (1.78x) → @35K=41.2% (1.71x) → @45K=69.3% (2.09x) (accelerating overestimation) |\n| Both trained dt_emb → accelerating v/e | exp_006 (H=15) vs exp_008d (H=8) | 006: v/e @35K=31.1% (1.29x)→@45K=53.3% (1.61x)→@55K=93.3% (2.31x); 008d: v/e @35K=41.2% (1.71x)→@45K=69.3% (2.09x) — both show accelerating normalized v/e leading to collapse |\n| Baseline v/e calibration (overshoot reference) | exp_001_baseline | v/e@35K=24.1%, @45K=33.1%, @55K=40.4%. Overshoot ratio: 008d@35K=1.7x, @45K=2.1x; 006@45K=1.6x, @55K=2.3x (all >1.5x = pathological) |\n\n**Strength**: Strong. The 008c vs 008d comparison is a controlled experiment isolating dt_embedding training as the single variable. The v/e overshoot ratio (experiment v/e / baseline v/e at same step) quantitatively identifies pathological regimes: trained dt_emb variants exceed 1.5x baseline before collapse, while untrained variants stay at or below baseline levels. **Pending confirmation**: exp_008f (dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON) will isolate whether dt_embedding conditioning or RSSM's learned dt=2 dynamics is the true cause.\n\n### C3: Untrained dt_embedding prevents optimistic drift, substantively protecting performance\n\nWhen dt_embedding is untrained (random fixed), the value function cannot exploit precise dt information, preventing the optimistic value drift seen in trained variants. This value growth suppression substantively protects performance: exp_008a demonstrates two complete V-shaped recovery cycles over 105K steps (peak @105K=778, 85% of baseline 916), with normalized v/e consistently suppressed at 0.59-0.93x baseline. The trained dt_embedding variant (exp_006) collapses catastrophically as its v/e ratio accelerates far past baseline levels (2.3x baseline@55K).\n\n| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n|----------|-----------|------------|\n| Two V-shaped recoveries (105K) | exp_008a (dt=2, subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=15) | 501→563→488→608→470→584→572→778; two complete recovery cycles over 105K steps. @65K=608 (-1.3% baseline), @105K=778 (-15.1% baseline, 85% of 916). No collapse. |\n| Sustained v/e suppression | exp_008a | v/e: 37.6%@55K → 37.2%@65K → 53.6%@75K → 47.5%@85K → 49.7%@95K → 38.6%@105K. Normalized v/e: 0.93x→0.66x→0.75x→0.68x→0.79x→0.59x baseline. Consistently below 1.0x, no acceleration. |\n| Trained dt_emb: accelerating collapse | exp_006 (dt=2, subsample ON, trained dt_emb, H=15) | 485→477→360→collapse; v/e: 53.3%@45K (1.61x)→93.3%@55K (2.31x) → immediate collapse |\n| v/e rate comparison (H=8 controlled) | exp_008c vs exp_008d | 008c (untrained): @35K=21.8% (0.90x)→@65K=32.8% (0.58x) (normalized declining); 008d (trained): @25K=15.5% (1.78x)→@35K=41.2% (1.71x) (normalized >1.5x = pathological). ~7x slower overestimation rate |\n| Baseline v/e calibration | exp_001_baseline | v/e: 8.7%@25K → 24.1%@35K → 40.4%@55K → 56.3%@65K → 65.6%@105K (stable 69-72% from 135K+). 008a normalized v/e: 0.93x@55K → 0.66x@65K → 0.59x@105K (suppressed, diverging further below baseline); 008d: 1.7x@35K → 2.1x@45K (optimistic drift) |\n\n**Strength**: Strong (B+ confirmed with 105K long-run data). Two complete V-shaped recovery cycles (501→608→470→778) with normalized v/e consistently 0.59-0.93x baseline across 105K steps. This is structural value growth suppression, not a transient delay. Contrasts sharply with exp_006's accelerating v/e (1.6x→2.3x baseline → collapse). The mechanism is clear: untrained dt_embedding prevents the value function from exploiting precise (but wrong) dt>1 predictions, suppressing the optimistic value drift that drives the delusional critic feedback loop in trained variants.\n\n**Diagnostic metric: v/e overshoot ratio** = experiment v/e / baseline v/e at same training step. >1.5x = pathological warning. Trained dt_emb variants: 008d@35K=1.7x, @45K=2.1x; 006@45K=1.6x, @55K=2.3x. Untrained: 008a normalized v/e range 0.59-0.93x over 55K-105K (consistently below baseline = healthy, diverging further from baseline over time).\n\n**105K long-run confirmed**: exp_008a ran to 112K steps. Normalized v/e at 105K=0.59x baseline (lowest point), confirming value growth suppression is structural, not a transient delay. The suppression strengthens over time rather than converging to baseline levels.\n\n### C4: Longer dt amplifies the problem\n\nIncreasing dt from 2 to 4 worsens degradation, consistent with RSSM prediction error compounding over longer temporal gaps.\n\n| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n|----------|-----------|------------|\n| dt=2 degradation | exp_006_fixed_dt2 | Peak 485, collapse to ~135 |\n| dt=4 severe degradation | exp_007_fixed_dt4 | Peak 176.9@25K, 144.4@45K (33% of baseline@45K=443) |\n| Monotonic relationship | dt=1 (~950) > dt=2 (peak 485@35K) > dt=4 (peak 177@25K) | Clear monotonic decline |\n\n**Strength**: Moderate. Only two dt values tested (2 and 4). The monotonic trend is clear but a finer grid (dt=3, dt=6) would strengthen this claim. Sufficient for a supporting claim but not a standalone finding.\n\n### C5: Learning signal reduction from shorter effective horizons compounds degradation but is not the root cause\n\nSubsampling with dt>1 reduces the effective number of learning transitions per episode. This contributes to degradation but is neither necessary nor sufficient for collapse.\n\n| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n|----------|-----------|------------|\n| Subsample OFF, still degraded | exp_008c (subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=8) | eval ~242 vs baseline ~950 |\n| Subsample OFF, no collapse | exp_008a (subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=15) | eval 778@105K (85% baseline), no collapse through 112K steps |\n| Subsample ON, collapse | exp_008d (subsample ON, trained dt_emb, H=8) | eval 146, value overestimation |\n| Horizon effect | exp_008c (H=8) vs exp_008a (H=15) | H=15 significantly outperforms H=8, both subsample OFF |\n\n**Strength**: Moderate. The 008c vs 008a comparison shows horizon length matters independently. But disentangling horizon from subsample effects requires additional controls. The key point—that it's not the root cause—is well-supported by 008c's stability despite lower performance.\n\n---\n\n## Story Arc\n\n### 1. Introduction\n- Temporal abstraction is a long-sought goal in RL (options, macro-actions, skip connections)\n- World-model RL (DreamerV3) offers a natural testbed: modify imagination dt without changing environment interaction\n- Puzzle: all our attempts at variable-rate imagination degrade performance. Why?\n- Contribution: systematic factorial diagnosis identifying trained dt_embedding → delusional critic as the root cause\n\n### 2. Background & Related Work\n- Temporal abstraction in model-free RL (options framework, FiGAR, action repeat)\n- World-model RL (Dreamer family, IRIS, TWM)\n- Variable-rate planning in world models (few prior works, mostly positive framing)\n- Value overestimation / delusional policies in model-based RL\n\n### 3. Methodology\n- DreamerV3 as base architecture\n- Variable-rate imagination: dt_embedding, temporal subsampling, learned gating\n- **Factorial experiment design**: 2×2×2 grid (dt_embedding trained/untrained × subsample ON/OFF × H=8/15) + baselines\n- Diagnostic metrics: eval return, value/eval ratio as overestimation proxy, learning curves\n\n### 4. Results\n- **Finding 1**: All dt>1 configurations degrade (C1)\n- **Finding 2**: Controlled ablation isolates trained dt_embedding (C2) — the \"smoking gun\" comparison (008c vs 008d)\n- **Finding 3**: Untrained dt_embedding prevents optimistic drift, sustaining near-baseline performance (C3)\n- **Finding 4**: Longer dt amplifies (C4)\n- **Finding 5**: Horizon/subsample effects are secondary (C5)\n\n### 5. Discussion\n- Mechanism: why trained dt_embedding causes delusional critic (RSSM fidelity gap at dt>1)\n- Connection to existing theory: delusional policies (Delalleau et al.), model exploitation in MBRL\n- Why this is specific to world-model RL (model-free temporal abstraction doesn't suffer the same failure mode)\n\n### 6. Implications for Future Work\n- Don't train dt_embedding jointly with value function in current world-model architectures\n- RSSM prediction quality must improve before variable-rate imagination is viable\n- Value growth suppression (e.g., untrained dt_embedding) as a potential mitigation direction\n- Need for diagnostic methodology in temporal abstraction research\n\n---\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n### R1: \"Limited to one environment / one base algorithm\"\n**Pre-emption**: Our claims are mechanistic (trained dt_embedding → value overestimation → collapse). The causal chain is architecture-specific by design—we diagnose *why* it fails in DreamerV3, not whether it fails everywhere. The mechanism (RSSM fidelity gap) likely generalizes to other latent-dynamics models but we scope claims conservatively.\n**Mitigation**: Cheetah Run is a planned experiment in our experiment schedule, not a stretch goal. We will include at least one additional DMC environment (Cheetah Run) to demonstrate generality of the mechanism.\n\n### R2: \"No proposed solution — what's the actionable takeaway?\"\n**Pre-emption**: Diagnostic papers serve a different purpose than method papers. Identifying root causes (trained dt_embedding) and quantitative signatures (v/e overshoot ratio >1.5x baseline = pathological) gives the community concrete guidance. We explicitly outline mitigation directions (value growth suppression, improved RSSM, decoupled dt_embedding training).\n**Mitigation**: Frame implications section as a \"research agenda\" with specific, testable hypotheses.\n\n### R3: \"Value/eval ratio is a crude proxy for overestimation\"\n**Pre-emption**: We acknowledge this is a proxy, not a formal divergence measure. However, the v/e overshoot ratio (experiment v/e / baseline v/e at same step) consistently identifies pathological overestimation: trained dt_emb variants exceed 1.5x baseline v/e before collapse, while untrained variants stay at or below baseline levels.\n**Mitigation**: Add distributional analysis of value predictions vs. realized returns if time permits.\n\n### R4: \"The factorial design is incomplete — missing cells in the grid\"\n**Pre-emption**: We prioritized the most informative comparisons. The 008c vs 008d pair isolates dt_embedding training with all else held constant—this is the critical controlled experiment.\n**Mitigation**: Explicitly present the factorial grid, mark which cells are filled, and justify the prioritization.\n\n### R5: \"Novelty concern — model exploitation / value overestimation in MBRL is well-known\"\n**Pre-emption**: General MBRL overestimation is known (Janner et al., 2019), but the specific mechanism through temporal abstraction's dt_embedding is novel. Prior work on temporal abstraction in world models has not identified this failure mode. Our contribution is the *specific causal link*, not the general phenomenon.\n\n### R6: \"All results from a single seed — how robust are the conclusions?\"\n**Pre-emption**: Our claims are about *mechanisms* (causal chain from dt_embedding → value overestimation → collapse), not about precise numerical thresholds. The mechanism manifests consistently across all configurations (exp_005, 006, 007, 008d) — four independent experiments all show the same value/eval ratio divergence pattern. The probability of this pattern appearing by chance across 4 experiments is negligible.\n**Mitigation**: Planned multi-seed runs for final paper. The factorial design (008c vs 008d) provides cross-experiment replication of the core mechanism.\n\n### R7: \"The factorial design confounds dt_embedding training with training data composition\"\n**Pre-emption**: We acknowledge this confound between 008c (subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb) and 008d (subsample ON, trained dt_emb). Experiment 008f (dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON) is designed to resolve this: it trains with dt=2 transitions (like 008d) but without dt_embedding conditioning. If 008f collapses → the cause is RSSM's learned dt=2 dynamics, not dt_embedding per se. If 008f remains stable → dt_embedding conditioning is confirmed as the root cause.\n**Mitigation**: exp_008f is a blocking experiment for the final paper. Results will be available before submission.\n\n---\n\n## Experiment Coverage Assessment\n\n| Claim | Evidence Status | Gaps |\n|-------|----------------|------|\n| C1 (degradation) | ✅ Strong — 3 configurations (005, 006, 007) all negative | Could add 1 more environment |\n| C2 (root cause: dt_emb) | ⚠️ Provisional — pending exp_008f to resolve dt_embedding vs training data confound | Consider adding value prediction distribution analysis |\n| C3 (preventing optimistic drift) | ✅ Strong (105K confirmed) — 008a@105K=778 (85% baseline), normalized v/e=0.59x, two V-shaped recoveries | None — long-term structural suppression confirmed |\n| C4 (dt amplification) | ⚠️ Moderate — only dt=2 vs dt=4 | Would benefit from dt=3, but not blocking |\n| C5 (horizon/subsample) | ⚠️ Moderate — confounded with other factors | Need 008c-equivalent with H=15 + subsample ON + untrained dt_emb for clean isolation |\n\n### Priority Actions Before Submission\n1. ~~**Check exp_008a@65K**~~ — ✅ Done: 608 (-1.3% baseline), B+ confirmed\n2. **Complete factorial grid analysis** — present all 8 cells, even if some are interpolated\n3. **Value prediction distribution plots** — strengthen C2 beyond ratio proxy\n4. **Second environment** (stretch goal) — addresses R1\n\n---\n\n## Key Figures (Planned)\n\n1. **Figure 1**: Learning curves — all experiments overlaid, showing degradation pattern (hero figure)\n2. **Figure 2**: Value/eval ratio over training — separating healthy vs. pathological regimes\n3. **Figure 3**: Factorial grid summary — 2×2 (dt_emb × subsample) with H as secondary axis\n4. **Figure 4**: Causal diagram — dt_embedding → value overestimation → actor degradation → collapse\n5. **Figure 5**: dt=1 vs dt=2 vs dt=4 comparison — monotonic degradation (C4)\n","numLines":192,"startLine":1,"totalLines":192}}}
